Jared's all squeezing my brain with the headphones here in New York.
杰瑞德在纽约这边把耳机调得紧紧的，挤得我脑壳疼。

90
00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.540
Should we go into Fast Facts?
我们要进入“快速事实”环节吗？

91
00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:04.520
I think we should.
我觉得应该。

92
00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:05.280
All right.
好的。

93
00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.720
Fast fact number one.
快速事实第一条。

94
00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:12.060
You might remember, because we shared this earlier, that NBC ordered 28 episodes for
你们可能还记得，因为我们之前分享过，NBC当时预订了28集

95
00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:12.700
season five.
第五季。

96
00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.140
It was our longest season.
那是我们最长的一季。

97
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.360
I remember, Jenna, when we wrapped season five, we all got sick.
我记得，珍娜，当我们拍完第五季时，我们都病倒了。

98
00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:20.560
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

99
00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.540
Like, we all got the flu or something.
就像是，我们都得了流感之类的。

100
00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.860
Because I remember the next week, like, texting a few people.
因为我记得接下来的一周，我给几个人发了短信。

101
00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:25.780
I'm like, I have a cold.
我就说，我感冒了。

102
00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.040
And Kate was like, yeah, me too.
凯特就说，是啊，我也是。

103
00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.460
Like, I think our bodies were just like.
感觉我们的身体当时就是那种状态。

104
00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:29.460
Yeah.
没错。

105
00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:35.840
A standard network television season usually runs on television from September to May.
标准的电视网剧集通常从九月播到五月。

106
00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.700
We work from July to March, right?
我们是从七月拍到三月，对吧？

107
00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:41.620
So that we can get the episodes ready.
这样我们才能把剧集准备好。

108
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.940
And a standard television schedule is usually where you do three weeks on, one week off
标准的电视制作周期通常是拍三周，休一周。

109
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:49.840
of filming.
拍摄的话。

110
00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.840
So usually a show will take one hiatus week a month.
所以通常剧组每个月会休假一周。

111
00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.760
But the writers always continue to work for that week.
但编剧们在那一周总是继续工作。

112
00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:02.900
That week off is meant so that the writers and the producer, they have a sort of catch-up week.
那一周的休息是为了让编剧和制片人有一个缓冲周。

113
00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.260
Because they're constantly writing, prepping, editing, delivering the episodes.
因为他们一直在写剧本、筹备、剪辑、交付剧集。

114
00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:10.380
They would have these episodes in multiple forMs.
他们同时要处理好几集的内容。

115
00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.720
They're, like, doing an outline for one, but they're writing another.
他们可能在写这一集的提纲，同时又在写另一集的剧本。

116
00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.180
They're punching up another one.
还在润色另一集。

117
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.180
They're doing post-editing on another one.
还在做另一集的后期剪辑。

118
00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.340
They've got, like, five episodes going at once.
他们同时得忙活五集的内容。

119
00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.080
We would just, like, be like, what are we filming this week?
我们当时就只会问，这周拍什么？

120
00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:31.040
This year, with this crazy 28-episode season, Steve Carell also had a commitment to do a film.
今年，因为这疯狂的28集拍摄季，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔还要去拍一部电影。

121
00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.660
I think it was Get Smart.
我想应该是《糊涂侦探》。

122
00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:38.900
And he needed, like, a six- to eight-week break from the show in the middle of that July-to-March
他需要在七月到三月的拍摄周期中间，

123
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.080
filming schedule so he could film Get Smart.
请六到八周的假去拍《糊涂侦探》。

124
00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.680
How did we ever do that?
我们当时是怎么撑过来的？

125
00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:47.980
In order to do that, we had to film 19 episodes in a row.
为了做到这一点，我们必须连续拍摄19集。

126
00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:49.980
That's when we got sick.
那时候我们都病倒了。

127
00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.900
That's when we got sick.
那时候我们都病倒了。

128
00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.700
I just have a memory of a bunch of us getting a cold bug.
我记得我们当时好多人都染上了感冒病毒。

129
00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.320
That was it.
就是那样。

130
00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:57.960
Yeah.
没错。

131
00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:03.800
So Frame Toby was right in the middle of this crazy 19-episode schedule.
所以《陷害托比》那一集正好就在这疯狂的19集拍摄期中间。

132
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:04.840
Oy, oy, oy.
哎呀，哎呀，哎呀。

133
00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.040
And here's why I think this is significant.
这就是为什么我觉得这很重要。

134
00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:15.840
It's really crazy to me that they decided to bring Toby back in the middle of this 19-episode stretch.
让我觉得不可思议的是，他们竟然决定在这19集的拍摄间隙把托比带回来。

135
00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.440
Because remember, he was now our showrunner because Greg was doing Parks and Rec.
因为要记住，他当时已经是我们的剧集运作人了，因为格雷格在忙《公园与游憩》。

136
00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:25.200
So Paul Lieberstein is now showrunning and acting in an episode.
所以保罗·李伯斯坦当时既要负责剧集运作，又要出演那一集。

137
00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.540
Again, because they gave him that break.
再说一次，因为他们给了他那个休息机会。

138
00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.460
And now they're like, sorry, bud.
结果现在他们又说，抱歉，伙计。

139
00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.040
You need to be Toby again.
你得变回托比了。

140
00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.180
You're back in the mix.
你又得回到这个圈子里了。

141
00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.260
So I reached out to Jen Salata, who was running the show with him.
所以我联系了当时和他一起负责剧集的珍·萨拉塔。

142
00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:38.360
And I said, do you know why you did that?
我问她，你知道你们当时为什么要那样做吗？

143
00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.620
Did you just want Paul to never sleep?
你们是不是就是想让保罗永远没觉睡？

144
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.040
What was your plan there?
你们当时的计划是什么？

145
00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:47.720
And she said she can't remember exactly the reasoning, but because Holly had left,
她说她记不清具体原因了，但因为霍莉离开了，

146
00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.660
they were either going to have to cast someone new or bring Toby back.
他们要么得选个新角色，要么就得把托比带回来。

147
00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.120
And that dynamic between Toby and Michael was so beloved.
而托比和迈克尔之间的那种互动太受欢迎了。

148
00:05:55.300 --> 00:06:00.180
She said as a fan of the show, she wanted Toby to come back to that role.
她说作为剧集的粉丝，她希望托比能回归那个角色。

149
00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:06.340
As a co-showrunner, she was freaked out at the idea of Paul having to wear both hats.
但作为联合剧集运作人，她对保罗要身兼两职感到非常焦虑。

150
00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.300
But she said he did it so well.
但她说他完成得非常出色。

151
00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:11.580
And Paul said he doesn't remember sleeping a lot.
保罗说他不记得自己睡了很多觉。

152
00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:12.340
Aw.
噢。

153
00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.200
But also, he enjoyed doing it.
但同时，他也很享受那个过程。

154
00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:17.380
You know, he liked his time on set with us.
你知道，他很喜欢和我们一起在片场度过的时光。

155
00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:22.260
Well, I love Toby coming back just because watching Michael spiral is delicious.
嗯，我喜欢托比回来，仅仅是因为看着迈克尔抓狂太有意思了。

156
00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.200
This is one of my favorite episodes of the season for that reason.
正因如此，这是我本季最喜欢的剧集之一。

157
00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.740
So thank you, Paul, for doing that.
所以谢谢你，保罗，谢谢你这么做。

158
00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:30.660
But thank you.
但还是要谢谢你。

159
00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:36.300
My fast fact number two is a big thank you to James Carey,
我的第二个速记事实是特别感谢詹姆斯·凯里，

160
00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.580
because he gave us the shooting draft for Frame Toby.
因为他给了我们《陷害托比》的拍摄剧本。

161
00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:41.400
Yes, James.
没错，詹姆斯。

162
00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:44.500
This was so fun to watch it with the shooting draft.
拿着拍摄剧本看这一集真是太有趣了。

