00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:57.940
And that's my wedding dress.
那是我的婚纱。

339
00:12:58.140 --> 00:12:59.320
There it is.
原来如此。

340
00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:03.540
I wonder how many more of these that you won.
我好奇你还赢过多少次这种比赛。

341
00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:07.720
I wonder, were you a big winner in your mind as the character of Angela?
我很好奇，作为安吉拉这个角色，你觉得她当时是个大赢家吗？

342
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.920
Do you think she won quite often?
你觉得她经常赢吗？

343
00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:11.080
Yes.
是的。

344
00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:13.980
I think that Angela Martin, like, peaked at 13.
我觉得安吉拉·马丁的人生巅峰大概是在13岁。

345
00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:14.780
Okay.
好吧。

346
00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.540
Like, she was it.
就像，那是她的高光时刻。

347
00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:22.300
She won all of, like, the young pageant, junior pageant, and then she retired.
她赢得了所有那些幼年、少年的选美比赛，然后就退役了。

348
00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:23.020
I see.
我明白了。

349
00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:23.940
Okay.
好的。

350
00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:24.980
Let us move on.
我们继续吧。

351
00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:29.980
While we're in the conference room, Kelly is going to take two brownies.
当我们还在会议室的时候，凯莉拿了两块布朗尼。

352
00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.200
One for Toby.
一块给托比。

353
00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:31.940
Right.
没错。

354
00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:32.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

355
00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:37.140
And Michael kind of scoffs at this, but nobody else seems to think it's a joke.
迈克尔对此嗤之以鼻，但其他人似乎并不觉得这是个笑话。

356
00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.980
Yeah, he calls her a weirdo.
是啊，他叫她怪胎。

357
00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:40.560
He's like, whatever, weirdo.
他就像是说，随便吧，怪胎。

358
00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:41.400
I know.
我知道。

359
00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:44.380
And Jim is like, Michael, Toby is back.
吉姆就说，迈克尔，托比回来了。

360
00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.360
And Michael's like, okay.
迈克尔就说，好吧。

361
00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:50.760
And so he walks back to the annex, and no one's there.
于是他走回办公区，那里没人。

362
00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.640
But then suddenly someone is there, and it is Toby.
但突然有人在那儿了，是托比。

363
00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:55.820
It is Toby.
真的是托比。

364
00:13:55.820 --> 00:14:02.500
Toby, I want you guys to know at one minute, 23 seconds, as Michael turns to see Toby, and
托比，我想让你们知道，在1分23秒时，当迈克尔转头看到托比，

365
00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.660
he has that look of horror in his face.
他脸上露出了那种惊恐的表情。

366
00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:11.960
If you look at the wall behind him, you will see that there are three framed sort of things
如果你看他身后的墙，你会发现墙上挂着三个装裱好的东西，

367
00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:12.940
on the wall for Toby.
是给托比的。

368
00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:19.640
There is an award for Toby Flindersen, a certificate of achievement, and a diploma from the California
有一个托比·弗林德森的奖项，一张成就证书，还有一个加州海岸学院的文凭。

369
00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:20.960
Coastal College.
所以，珍娜，他回来已经有一段时间了，足够把这些装裱好的东西挂起来。

370
00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:24.860
So, Jenna, he had been back long enough to hang up his framed iteMs.
在剧本里，托比有一个采访镜头，他说过这样的话，

371
00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:29.120
And in the script, Toby had a talking head where he said this,
我已经回来六天了。

372
00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.840
I've been back for six days.
我想我甚至都跟他谈过了。

373
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.560
I think I've even talked to him.
真希望那段保留下来了。

374
00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:33.760
I wish that stayed in.
我也是。

375
00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:34.320
Me too.
我太希望它能保留下来了。

376
00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.320
I wish so much it had stayed in.
关于我的背景细节，各位，加州海岸学院，我觉得那不是个真实存在的学校。

377
00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:41.820
For my background catch, folks, the California Coastal College, I don't think that's a thing.
我谷歌了一下。

378
00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:42.580
I googled it.
没找到。

379
00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:43.400
I couldn't find it.
我确实找到了加州海岸大学，那是一所位于加州圣安娜的私立在线大学。

380
00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:50.580
I did find the California Coast University, which is a private online university based
哦。

381
00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:52.060
in Santa Ana, California.
原来如此。

382
00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:52.800
Oh.
这就是我的背景调查，各位。

383
00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:53.640
There you go.
好吧，我们收到了很多粉丝来信。

384
00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:54.700
My background, people.
大家想知道迈克尔大喊“不”以及所有那些反应是即兴发挥的，还是剧本里写的。

385
00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:56.560
Well, we got a lot of fan mail.
在剧本里，只写了迈克尔转身尖叫，用的是大写字母。

386
00:14:56.800 --> 00:15:03.520
People wanted to know if Michael's screaming no and all of that was improvised or if it was
没错。

387
00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:04.240
in the script.
但那整段“不，不，上帝，不”，那是史蒂夫自己加的。

388
00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:09.860
In the script, it just says Michael turns and screams in all caps.
那是史蒂夫对剧本提示的演绎。

389
00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:10.400
Yeah.
那有多好笑啊？

390
00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:14.360
But that whole, like, no, no, God, no, that was Steve.
伙计们，如果剧本写着让你尖叫，我想我们大多数人只会喊一声“啊”，对吧？

391
00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.280
That was Steve's interpretation of that script note.
是的。

392
00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.060
And how funny was that?
但史蒂夫把那一刻演绎得淋漓尽致。

393
00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:24.960
You guys, if you read that you scream, I think most of us would just be like, ah, right?
以最好的方式。

394
00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:25.440
Yes.
他真是个喜剧天才。

395
00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:28.120
But Steve made a meal out of that moment.
没错。

396
00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.560
In the best way.
你知道吗，Screen Rant列出了《办公室》创造的15大流行文化梗，

397
00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.480
He's a comedy genius.
史蒂夫喊“不”的那个表情包就是其中之一。

398
00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:32.240
Yes.
是的。

399
00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:38.420
You know, Screen Rant did a list of the top 15 pop culture references created by The Office
我太希望它能保留下来了。

400
00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:42.120
and the meme of Steve saying no is one of them.
我太希望它能保留下来了。

401
00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:43.340
I don't doubt it.
我对此深信不疑。

402
00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:48.620
I have been online where I see people that I don't even know, like, respond to other people
我上网时看到一些我根本不认识的人，比如，回复别人

403
00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:50.460
with just Steve's face going, no.
只发一张史蒂夫的脸，写着“不”。

404
00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:51.820
It's amazing.
太神奇了。

405
00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.560
Well, the episode starts and Michael is spiraling.
嗯，剧集开始时，迈克尔正处于崩溃边缘。

406
00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:56.900
He's going to call David Wallace.
他打算给大卫·华莱士打电话。

407
00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:02.480
He's watching stupid Toby as he shows his stupid photos of Costa Rica to Phyllis.
他看着愚蠢的托比向菲利斯展示他那些愚蠢的哥斯达黎加照片。

408
00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:03.140
Yeah.
没错。

409
00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:07.340
He manages to get David on the phone by texting him 911.
他通过给大卫发“911”短信成功联系上了他。

410
00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.080
Call me.
给我回电话。

411
00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.180
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

412
00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:14.640
Michael said he's learned that people will not return his calls unless he texts 911.
迈克尔说他学到了一点，如果不发“911”短信，人们就不会回他电话。

413
00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:18.320
And now everybody does because they think something horrible has happened.
现在每个人都会回了，因为他们以为发生了什么可怕的事。

414
00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:18.820
So.
所以。

415
00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:21.160
I had a pager when I first got to L.A.
我刚到洛杉矶时有个寻呼机。

416
00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.340
So did I.
我也是。

417
00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:23.220
You had to.
那时候必须得有。

418
00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:23.760
I know.
我知道。

419
00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:26.000
Because you didn't, like, really have cell phones.
因为那时候还没怎么普及手机。

420
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:26.980
You had a pager.
你得有个寻呼机。

421
00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:33.020
And the only reason you had a pager was so that your agent could page you if you got
而且你用寻呼机的唯一原因，就是为了让经纪人在有试镜机会时

422
00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:33.600
an audition.
能呼你。

423
00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.900
And then you would have to go find a phone.
然后你就得去找电话。

424
00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:37.180
You'd have to find a pay phone.
你得找个公用电话。

425
00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:37.900
And call them back.
然后回拨给他们。

426
00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:38.260
Yeah.
没错。

427
00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:42.440
I used to keep a Ziploc bag full of change in my car for two reasons.
我以前车里总放着一个装满零钱的密封袋，有两个原因。

428
00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:47.800
One, for all of the metered parking that didn't accept credit cards, just coins.
第一，为了应付所有不接受信用卡、只收硬币的停车计时器。

429
00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:54.480
And two, so that I could find a pay phone and call my agent back when my agent paged
第二，为了在经纪人呼我的时候，能找到公用电话回电，

430
00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:56.600
me, which was maybe twice a year.
虽然一年可能也就两次。

431
00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:57.320
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

432
00:16:57.460 --> 00:17:02.040
I remember one time distinctly, I was driving through Santa Monica with some friends and
我清楚地记得有一次，我和朋友开车经过圣莫尼卡，

433
00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:04.740
my pager went off and I almost swerved off the road.
我的寻呼机响了，我差点把车开出路面。

434
00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:08.980
Because I was like, what is happening?
因为我当时想，发生什么事了？

435
00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:11.320
I've hit the big time.
我终于出人头地了。

436
00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:12.340
I've been paged.
我接到呼叫了。

437
00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:13.960
We were supposed to be going to the beach.
我们本来打算去海滩的。

438
00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:15.160
So I was like, no, we can't do that now.
所以我说，不行，现在不能去了。

439
00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:15.960
I have to find a pay phone.
我得找个公用电话。

440
00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:18.240
So we're all like driving the streets looking for a pay phone.
于是我们都在街上开车找公用电话。

441
00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:18.940
I pulled over.
我靠边停车。

442
00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.280
I ran up to the pay phone.
我跑向公用电话。

443
00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:22.380
I put my quarters in, called them.
我投进硬币，给他们打了过去。

444
00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:28.480
And they were like, all right, have you ever needed any kind of glasses?
结果他们说，好吧，你以前需要戴眼镜吗？

445
00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.220
I'm like, what?
我说，什么？

446
00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:31.580
No.
不需要。

447
00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:34.500
And they're like, we have an audition for you for Lens Crafters.
他们说，我们有个Lens Crafters的试镜机会。

448
00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:36.140
They would like people who wear glasses.
他们想要戴眼镜的人。

449
00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:37.880
I'm like, that's not me.
我说，那不是我。

450
00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:38.640
All right.
好吧。

451
00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:39.120
Bye.
再见。

452
00:17:40.340 --> 00:17:43.620
Yeah, that's pretty much it.
对，差不多就是这样。

453
00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:48.520
But then I did have a boyfriend once who was not calling me back.
但我确实有个男朋友曾经不回我电话。

454
00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:50.640
Did you light up that pager?
你狂轰滥炸他的传呼机了吗？

455
00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:53.940
I sure did with a bunch of 911s.
我当然有，发了一堆911。

456
00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:54.760
You know it.
你懂的。

457
00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.300
Did you really, Jenna?
你真的做了吗，珍娜？

458
00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:56.820
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

459
00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:57.920
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

460
00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:59.040
I did.
我做了。

461
00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.800
Were you a psycho girlfriend?
你当时是个疯狂的女友吗？

462
00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:02.440
You know what?
你知道吗？

463
00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:04.280
He was cheating on me that night.
那天晚上他出轨了。

464
00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:05.820
Oh, so you knew.
哦，所以你当时就知道。

465
00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:06.780
You knew.
你早就知道了。

466
00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:07.980
I knew it.
我确实知道。

467
00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.600
We broke up after that.
那之后我们就分手了。

468
00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.260
Oh, man.
天哪。

469
00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:11.920
Yeah.
是啊。

470
00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.500
I wouldn't light up the pager.
我不会去狂轰滥炸传呼机。

471
00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:15.280
I'm like sitting here calling you psycho.
我坐在这儿说你是疯狂女友。

472
00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:19.240
I wouldn't light up the pager, but I would drive over and like hide out in a bush.
我不会去狂轰滥炸传呼机，但我会开车过去，躲在灌木丛里。

473
00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:23.240
That's so much more elaborate than texting 911.
那可比发911短信复杂多了。

474
00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:25.000
Here was my plan.
我的计划是这样的。

475
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.960
I was like, I know he's cheating on me.
我当时想，我知道他在出轨。

476
00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:32.040
So I'm going to light up that pager and make it buzz so that while they're whatever they're
所以我打算狂轰滥炸那个传呼机，让它一直响，这样当他们正在做那什么的时候，

477
00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:38.540
doing, the pagers is like, yeah, I'm just going to ruin their good time.
传呼机就在那响，我就想，没错，我就是要搅了他们的好事。

478
00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:40.240
He probably just turned it off.
他可能直接关机了。

479
00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:43.980
I guess I'm just going to jump out of a bush and be like, hey, what are you doing?
我猜我只能从灌木丛里跳出来说，嘿，你们在干嘛？

480
00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:44.420
Gotcha.
抓到你了。

481
00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:50.380
Now I'm going to go home because I've got twigs in my hair and I'm embarrassed.
现在我要回家了，因为我头发里全是树枝，而且我很尴尬。

482
00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.940
Is this a plot line for mom detectives?
这是《妈妈侦探》的剧情线吗？

483
00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:57.860
Should we set mom detectives in the past where all we have are pagers and bush hiding?
我们应该把《妈妈侦探》设定在过去吗？那时候我们只有传呼机和躲灌木丛。

484
00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:58.420
Yes.
是的。

485
00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:00.640
Oh, bush hiding.
哦，躲灌木丛。

486
00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:02.240
Uh-oh.
呃哦。

487
00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:04.940
That could be something else.
那听起来可能有点别的意思。

488
00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:06.420
What's wrong with this?
这有什么问题吗？

489
00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:07.920
Can we call it bush hiders?
我们能叫它《灌木躲藏者》吗？

490
00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:08.780
No.
不行。

491
00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:11.620
We can't.
我们不能。

492
00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:13.140
It doesn't even make any sense.
这根本说不通。

493
00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.140
It doesn't make any sense.
这完全没道理。

494
00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:16.280
You go pitch it.
你去推销吧。

495
00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:17.140
Hi, our show.
嗨，我们的节目。

496
00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:18.460
It's called bush hiders.
它叫《灌木躲藏者》。

497
00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:22.360
And if you don't want to buy it, you're an a**hole because this is gold.
如果你不想买，那你就是个混蛋，因为这绝对是金牌剧本。

498
00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.100
And they're like, what's it about?
然后他们会问，这是讲什么的？

499
00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:26.240
And we're like, it's two mom detectives.
我们就说，这是两个妈妈侦探的故事。

500
00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:29.220
It's two older women in comfortable clothing.
是两个穿着舒适服装的中年女性。

