我们想要那种30分钟的换装环节。

503
00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.420
It won't be fitted.
衣服不会是合身的。

504
00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:41.140
And we want a lot of old tech that no one watching it will really understand.
而且我们想要很多没人看得懂的老式科技产品。

505
00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:42.960
And we're going to hide in some bushes.
我们还要躲在灌木丛里。

506
00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:43.720
Yeah.
没错。

507
00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:44.940
Do you want it?
你想要吗？

508
00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.100
Okay, where are we?
好了，我们讲到哪了？

509
00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:52.900
We shouldn't have shared that on the air because someone's going to steal it.
我们不该在节目里说出来的，因为肯定会有人去偷这个点子。

510
00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:57.920
I guarantee you, in two years, you're going to turn on HBO Max and there's going to be
我敢保证，两年后，你打开HBO Max，就会看到

511
00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:00.640
two 20-year-olds starring in a show called bush hiders.
两个20岁的年轻人主演了一部叫《灌木丛躲藏者》的剧。

512
00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:01.900
Mark my word.
走着瞧吧。

513
00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:03.660
Mark my word.
走着瞧吧。

514
00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:06.420
And they're going to be young, hot detectives in designer clothes.
而且他们会是穿着名牌服装的年轻火辣侦探。

515
00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:10.800
That's how it works in this business.
这行就是这么运作的。

516
00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:11.820
That's right.
没错。

517
00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.300
I'm not jaded.
我可没有变得愤世嫉俗。

518
00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:14.580
All right.
好吧。

519
00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:16.220
Should we move on?
我们要继续吗？

520
00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.420
What's happened to me in New York?
我在纽约到底怎么了？

521
00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.500
Who am I here?
我在这里是谁？

522
00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:19.440
I don't know.
我不知道。

523
00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:23.460
You just took a big swig of coffee and you're like, that's how it works in the business.
你刚才猛喝了一口咖啡，然后说，这行就是这么运作的。

524
00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:25.420
Well, listen, you know what?
好吧，听着，你知道吗？

525
00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:27.740
David Wallace tells Michael he's just going to have to deal with it.
大卫·华莱士告诉迈克尔，他只能接受这个事实。

526
00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:28.100
Yeah.
没错。

527
00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:32.100
And he couldn't believe that one of his employees had been back so long and he didn't know.
他简直不敢相信他的员工已经在后面待了那么久，而他竟然不知道。

528
00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:34.840
And Dwight and Michael let him know that the annex is icky.
德怀特和迈克尔告诉他，办公区附属地带很恶心。

529
00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:35.960
It's icky back there.
后面那地方很恶心。

530
00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:36.740
Yeah.
没错。

531
00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:40.380
And he really wants David to get rid of Toby.
而且他真的很想让大卫开除托比。

532
00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.740
And David says, I can't get rid of him without cause.
大卫说，没有正当理由我不能开除他。

533
00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:46.600
And Michael says, he has cause.
迈克尔说，他有正当理由。

534
00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:48.760
It's because I hate him.
理由就是我讨厌他。

535
00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:49.680
Because?
因为？

536
00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:52.740
But that is not obviously cause.
但这显然不是正当理由。

537
00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.240
Well, they're going to find something.
好吧，他们会找到理由的。

538
00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:56.880
But Jenna, another issue is happening.
但是珍娜，还有另一件事发生了。

539
00:20:57.240 --> 00:20:57.420
Yeah.
没错。

540
00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:59.580
It's a day of drama in the office.
办公室里充满戏剧性的一天。

541
00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:05.080
Pam is preparing food in the kitchen and she discovers a mess in the microwave.
帕姆在厨房准备食物，发现微波炉里一团糟。

542
00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:05.960
Jenna?
珍娜？

543
00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:06.440
Yeah.
在呢。

544
00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:08.120
Did you see what Pam was preparing?
你看到帕姆在准备什么了吗？

545
00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:10.200
I know what Pam was preparing.
我知道帕姆在准备什么。

546
00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:11.400
Share.
分享一下。

547
00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:17.620
This is maybe one of my most frequently asked questions outside of what was in the teapot note.
这可能是我被问到最多的问题之一，仅次于茶壶里的纸条写了什么。

548
00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:18.960
No way.
不会吧。

549
00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:19.480
Yes.
真的。

550
00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:24.760
People are like, what is Pam microwaving in the episode with the dirty microwave?
人们总是问，在微波炉很脏的那一集里，帕姆到底在用微波炉加热什么？

551
00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:26.300
Here are some guesses.
这里有一些猜测。

552
00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:27.360
We got mail.
我们收到邮件了。

553
00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:30.560
Here are what people are guessing that I was microwaving.
以下是大家猜测我当时在微波炉里热的东西。

554
00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:31.200
Okay.
好的。

555
00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:32.520
Apple juice.
苹果汁。

556
00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:32.880
Hmm.
嗯。

557
00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:34.760
A probiotic drink.
益生菌饮料。

558
00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:35.620
Okay.
好的。

559
00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:43.100
Egg whites, bone broth, soup, milk, porridge, and yogurt.
蛋清、骨汤、汤、牛奶、粥和酸奶。

560
00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.840
Well, I had no idea.
好吧，我完全没想到。

561
00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:46.800
So I looked at the script.
所以我看了看剧本。

562
00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.180
But Jenna, you tell us.
不过珍娜，还是你来告诉我们吧。

563
00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.620
It's egg whites.
是蛋清。

564
00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:55.220
It's egg whites, which I, by the way, knowing my BFF in real life, thought was kind of fitting.
是蛋清，顺便说一下，考虑到我在现实生活中是她的闺蜜，我觉得这还挺符合她的。

565
00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:56.240
Yeah.
没错。

566
00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:59.460
Because you can buy egg whites in these little cups.
因为你可以买到这种小杯装的蛋清。

567
00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:01.240
And that's what she's doing.
而她当时就在做这个。

568
00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.380
She's going to microwave herself some egg whites.
她打算给自己微波一份蛋清。

569
00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:07.220
A lot of people also asked, what was in the microwave?
还有很多人问，微波炉里装的是什么？

570
00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.340
That is also in the script.
剧本里也写了。

571
00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:10.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

572
00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:13.420
And it just says, like, a saucy mess, basically.
上面基本上就是写着，一团乱糟糟的酱汁。

573
00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:14.920
I typed it out.
我把它打出来了。

574
00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:20.520
It says, Pam opens the microwave door to put in some egg whites, but the microwave is splattered
上面写着，帕姆打开微波炉门准备放进一些蛋清，但微波炉里溅得

575
00:22:20.520 --> 00:22:22.320
all over with red sauce.
到处都是红色的酱汁。

576
00:22:22.600 --> 00:22:22.820
Yeah.
没错。

577
00:22:23.220 --> 00:22:24.760
Now we're in the break room.
现在我们到了休息室。

578
00:22:25.100 --> 00:22:26.900
And what would we title this?
我们该给这一段起什么标题呢？

579
00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:29.940
Jim's exposed in the break room?
吉姆在休息室暴露了？

580
00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:30.960
No, that doesn't sound good.
不，听起来不太好。

581
00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:32.240
Exposure in the break room.
休息室里的曝光事件。

582
00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:33.880
Exposure in the break room.
休息室里的曝光事件。

583
00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:36.600
Andy, I guess, has peepers like a hawk.
安迪，我想，他的眼睛像老鹰一样尖。

584
00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:41.740
And read Jim's email and found out that Jim is buying his parents' house and hasn't told
他读了吉姆的邮件，发现吉姆要买下他父母的房子，却还没告诉

585
00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:42.100
Pam.
帕姆。

586
00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:42.780
Yeah.
没错。

587
00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:46.240
Or as Kevin puts it, the same house he used to pee the bed in.
或者像凯文说的那样，就是他以前尿床的那栋房子。

588
00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:47.880
Phyllis thinks it's romantic.
菲利斯觉得这很浪漫。

589
00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.460
Until she asks Jim where it is.
直到她问吉姆房子在哪里。

590
00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:52.360
Jim says it's on Linden Ave.
吉姆说是林登大道。

591
00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:52.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

592
00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:54.320
And Phyllis makes a face.
然后菲利斯做了一个表情。

593
00:22:54.440 --> 00:22:57.760
And then in the background, you see me kind of roll my eyes like, ooh.
接着在背景里，你可以看到我翻了个白眼，大概是那种“噢”的感觉。

594
00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:00.560
I looked up Linden Ave in Scranton.
我查了一下斯克兰顿的林登大道。

595
00:23:00.680 --> 00:23:01.920
I couldn't find a Linden Ave.
我没找到林登大道。

596
00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:05.660
I found a Linden Street, but it's sort of like in the heart of the city.
我找到了林登街，但它大概是在市中心的位置。

597
00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:09.520
There's like shops and churches and definitely no quarry nearby.
那里有商店和教堂，附近绝对没有采石场。

598
00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:10.440
Oh.
噢。

599
00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:11.180
Hmm.
嗯。

600
00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:12.140
Interesting.
有意思。

601
00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:17.460
We got a lot of questions from, for example, Brittany Y and Jenner B.
我们收到了很多提问，比如来自 Brittany Y 和 Jenner B 的。

602
00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:20.560
Whose house did they use for Jim's parents' house?
吉姆父母家的房子用的是谁的家？

603
00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:26.020
Was the interior a set or was it the actual house that they used for the exterior?
室内是摄影棚搭建的，还是用了外景拍摄的那栋房子的内部？

604
00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:29.600
This is where Randy Cordray really came through for me, Ange.
这方面 Randy Cordray 真的帮了我大忙，Ange。

605
00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:30.960
Bring it home, Randy.
展示一下吧，Randy。

606
00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:34.720
I remembered that it was two different houses.
我记得那是两栋不同的房子。

607
00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:38.720
We used one for the interior and one for the exterior.
我们一栋用来拍室内，一栋用来拍室外。

608
00:23:39.040 --> 00:23:45.800
And Randy said that our location manager, Kyle Alexander, had found several choices and that
Randy 说我们的外景经理 Kyle Alexander 找了好几个选择，而且

609
00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:51.200
Randy had really hoped that they could find a single residence that they could do both
Randy 本来真的很希望他们能找到一栋房子，既能拍

610
00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:56.620
interior and exterior just because it would be so much easier to shoot at just one location.
室内又能拍室外，因为只在一个地方拍摄会方便得多。

611
00:23:56.620 --> 00:23:58.480
But it didn't work out that way.
但结果没能如愿。

612
00:23:58.480 --> 00:24:04.440
Randy said everything they looked at either worked for the interior but not the exterior or vice versa.
Randy 说他们看过的所有房子，要么室内合适但室外不行，要么反之。

613
00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:12.100
So for the exterior, we used an occupied home on Calvert Street in Van Nuys, California.
所以室外部分，我们用了加州范奈斯 Calvert 街上一户人家正在住的房子。

614
00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:16.540
But the interior was not suitable to shoot.
但室内不适合拍摄。

615
00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:20.380
This was because it was absolutely adorable inside.
这是因为里面装修得实在太可爱了。

616
00:24:20.660 --> 00:24:22.420
And it needed to look a little janky.
而我们需要它看起来稍微破旧一点。

617
00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:23.080
Yeah.
没错。

618
00:24:23.260 --> 00:24:24.200
It was so cute.
它太可爱了。

619
00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:29.700
And when we were shooting there, they would let John and I step in to the house to kind
我们在那里拍摄时，他们会让我们和 John 进屋，稍微

620
00:24:29.700 --> 00:24:31.640
of get our makeup refreshed and touched up.
补补妆，整理一下。

621
00:24:31.760 --> 00:24:34.640
But we would just stand right inside that front door.
但我们只会站在前门里面一点点的地方。

622
00:24:34.780 --> 00:24:36.700
And then we would go back outside again.
然后我们就又回到外面去了。

623
00:24:36.820 --> 00:24:37.880
And that was it.
仅此而已。

624
00:24:38.080 --> 00:24:39.260
And it was cute inside.
里面确实很可爱。

625
00:24:39.540 --> 00:24:40.040
Oh, my God.
天哪。

626
00:24:40.040 --> 00:24:40.980
It was so cute.
真的太可爱了。

627
00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:46.960
It was decorated like an English professor's home.
装修得就像一位英语教授的家。

628
00:24:46.960 --> 00:24:53.040
Like, just cozy, literary bookshelves.
就是那种温馨的、有书架的文学气息。

629
00:24:53.340 --> 00:24:57.020
Just beautiful kind of restored home inside.
室内就是那种装修得很漂亮的房子。

630
00:24:57.140 --> 00:24:57.940
So great.
太棒了。

631
00:24:58.300 --> 00:25:01.820
I did something similar one time on this show called Haters Back Off.
我以前在拍一部叫《喷子滚开》的剧时也遇到过类似的情况。

632
00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:04.560
We filmed the exterior in one house and the interior in another.
我们在一栋房子拍外景，在另一栋拍内景。

633
00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:08.780
And when we were filming the exterior, it was cold and kind of misty raining.
拍外景的时候，天气又冷又下着毛毛雨。

634
00:25:08.780 --> 00:25:11.840
And they let us step inside just the front room.
他们让我们进到前厅里避一避。

635
00:25:11.960 --> 00:25:12.520
Yeah, same.
是啊，我也是。

636
00:25:12.520 --> 00:25:13.420
We waited, right?
我们就在那儿等着，对吧？

637
00:25:13.600 --> 00:25:15.460
We didn't go throughout their house at all.
我们根本没在人家屋里到处走动。

638
00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:16.620
But we stepped in the front room.
但我们确实进了前厅。

639
00:25:16.620 --> 00:25:18.400
And I was with Steve Little.
当时我和 Steve Little 在一起。

640
00:25:18.400 --> 00:25:20.220
And we weren't really sure what to expect.
我们真的不知道会看到什么。

641
00:25:20.220 --> 00:25:21.760
We opened the door to step in.
我们推开门走进去。

642
00:25:22.140 --> 00:25:25.680
And there was maybe 4,000 tiny dolls.
结果里面大概有 4000 个小玩偶。

643
00:25:26.080 --> 00:25:26.540
What?
什么？

644
00:25:26.940 --> 00:25:27.380
Yes.
真的。

645
00:25:27.620 --> 00:25:27.920
What?
什么？

646
00:25:28.120 --> 00:25:31.380
There were dolls and cases, all kinds of fancy dolls.
到处都是玩偶和展示柜，各种精致的玩偶。

647
00:25:31.420 --> 00:25:33.240
And every kind of case you could imagine.
你能想象到的各种展示柜都有。

648
00:25:33.520 --> 00:25:34.660
Cases on the wall.
墙上有柜子。

649
00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:37.720
Little case stand on the ground.
地上有小柜子架。

650
00:25:37.720 --> 00:25:38.720
They were everywhere.
到处都是。

651
00:25:38.940 --> 00:25:41.480
And Steve and I stood right on the other side of the door.
当时我和史蒂夫就站在门的那一侧。

652
00:25:41.480 --> 00:25:44.640
And we're like, okay, so somebody likes dolls.
我们当时想，好吧，看来有人喜欢玩偶。

653
00:25:45.140 --> 00:25:45.980
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

654
00:25:46.100 --> 00:25:47.720
I would be like, run.
我要是遇到这种情况，肯定会跑。

655
00:25:48.240 --> 00:25:48.860
I know.
我也这么想。

656
00:25:49.460 --> 00:25:50.260
Run now.
赶紧跑。

657
00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:51.660
I was like, okay, all right.
我当时就想，好吧，行吧。

658
00:25:52.360 --> 00:25:57.300
If you have that many dolls, there's a very good chance that one of them is going to come alive and try to kill you.
如果你有那么多玩偶，很有可能其中一个会活过来并试图杀了你。

659
00:25:57.400 --> 00:26:00.800
I mean, if we've learned anything, one of them is possessed.
我是说，如果我们要从中学到什么的话，那就是其中一个肯定被附身了。

660
00:26:01.080 --> 00:26:02.120
One of them is possessed.
其中一个被附身了。

661
00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:03.360
And you know who's on the case?
你知道谁在调查这事吗？

662
00:26:03.500 --> 00:26:04.440
The mom detectives.
妈妈侦探团。

663
00:26:04.600 --> 00:26:05.300
The mom detectives.
妈妈侦探团。

664
00:26:05.300 --> 00:26:06.460
We got that covered.
这事儿我们包了。

665
00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:07.640
We got it covered.
我们搞得定。

666
00:26:07.640 --> 00:26:08.760
We'll hide in the bushes.
我们会躲在灌木丛里。

667
00:26:08.760 --> 00:26:09.740
We'll figure it out.
我们会查清楚的。

668
00:26:09.880 --> 00:26:10.580
That's right.
没错。

669
00:26:10.580 --> 00:26:13.140
So this house was so cute.
这房子真的很可爱。

670
00:26:13.380 --> 00:26:19.820
What Michael Gallenberg did, our set designer, he added a broken rain gutter to the outside.
我们的布景设计师迈克尔·加伦伯格在房子外面加了一个破损的雨水槽。

671
00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:24.960
He changed the front door so that it would match the other location.
他更换了前门，好让它与另一个拍摄地点匹配。

672
00:26:25.140 --> 00:26:25.440
Okay.
好的。

673
00:26:25.820 --> 00:26:26.760
Where we go inside.
就是我们进去的那个地方。

674
00:26:27.120 --> 00:26:31.960
And he also added that swinging screen door that bangs into the overhead awning.
他还加了那个会撞到上方遮阳棚的纱门。

675
00:26:32.280 --> 00:26:33.600
Oh, that was really funny.
哦，那个真的很有趣。

676
00:26:33.920 --> 00:26:34.640
I know.
我知道。

677
00:26:34.640 --> 00:26:43.440
And then they also asked the homeowner to turn off their sprinklers for a week leading up to the shoot to make the grass look kind of dry and weather-beaten.
他们还要求房主在拍摄前一周关掉喷水装置，让草坪看起来有些干枯、饱经风霜。

678
00:26:43.660 --> 00:26:44.680
And they did.
他们照做了。

679
00:26:44.680 --> 00:26:47.000
They kind of killed their lawn for us.
他们为了我们把草坪都弄死了。

680
00:26:47.120 --> 00:26:47.500
Thank you.
谢谢你们。

681
00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:57.080
Now, for the interior of Jim's parents' house and for the garage scenes, they found an unoccupied home on Allett Avenue, which is also in Van Nuys.
至于吉姆父母家的内部和车库场景，他们在范奈斯的阿莱特大道上找了一处空置的房子。

682
00:26:57.160 --> 00:26:59.340
It was only a few blocks away from the other house.
离另一栋房子只有几个街区远。

683
00:26:59.480 --> 00:27:01.580
And for this one, they went in.
对于这栋房子，他们进去了。

684
00:27:01.740 --> 00:27:03.300
They added the shag carpeting.
他们铺上了长毛地毯。

685
00:27:03.380 --> 00:27:04.720
They added the wood paneling.
他们装上了木镶板。

686
00:27:04.920 --> 00:27:06.440
They changed the front door.
他们换了前门。

687
00:27:06.640 --> 00:27:10.040
Like, they bought a front door, and they put it on both houses so it would match, you know?
他们买了一扇前门，装在两栋房子上，这样看起来就一样了，你懂吗？

688
00:27:10.040 --> 00:27:15.020
So, he was able to go in and completely set design the interior of the home.
所以，他能够进去并完全重新设计房子的内部布景。

689
00:27:15.240 --> 00:27:16.920
Is it A-L-L-O-T?
是拼写成A-L-L-O-T吗？

690
00:27:17.580 --> 00:27:19.280
A-L-L-O-T-T.
是A-L-L-O-T-T。

691
00:27:19.580 --> 00:27:22.260
And you say it Allot or Allett?
那你读作Allot还是Allett？

692
00:27:23.120 --> 00:27:23.840
All-ot.
All-ot。

693
00:27:24.460 --> 00:27:24.940
Allett?
Allett？

694
00:27:25.720 --> 00:27:26.200
Allett.
Allett。

695
00:27:27.160 --> 00:27:33.000
So, from everything I said, the thing that we're going to discuss is the street name and how to pronounce it.
所以，说了这么多，我们要讨论的重点竟然是这条街的名字以及怎么读它。

696
00:27:33.140 --> 00:27:34.180
Listen, I want you to know something.
听着，我想让你知道一件事。

697
00:27:34.180 --> 00:27:40.500
Whenever I think about, like, where I'm going to live, I think about the name of the street and having to tell it to, like, the pizza delivery guy.
每当我考虑要住哪里时，我都会想到街道的名字，以及以后得告诉送披萨的人地址。

698
00:27:41.080 --> 00:27:42.620
I live on Allot.
我住在Allot。

699
00:27:43.280 --> 00:27:43.720
Allot.
Allot。

700
00:27:43.840 --> 00:27:45.120
A-L-L-O-T.
A-L-L-O-T。

701
00:27:45.220 --> 00:27:46.240
No, not Allett.
不，不是Allett。

702
00:27:46.620 --> 00:27:47.460
Not Allett.
不是Allett。

703
00:27:47.940 --> 00:27:48.380
Allot.
是Allot。

704
00:27:48.980 --> 00:27:50.380
I play it out in my head.
我会在脑海里预演一遍。

705
00:27:50.460 --> 00:27:51.420
You guys don't do that?
你们不这样做吗？

706
00:27:51.880 --> 00:27:54.060
Clearly, you'd rather live on Calvert Street.
显然，你宁愿住在卡尔弗特街。

707
00:27:54.660 --> 00:27:55.100
Calvert.
卡尔弗特。

708
00:27:55.340 --> 00:27:55.700
Yes.
没错。

709
00:27:56.100 --> 00:27:58.600
Much easier for you to get your pizza on Calvert.
住在卡尔弗特街对你来说买披萨方便多了。

710
00:27:58.600 --> 00:27:59.080
That's right.
说得对。

711
00:27:59.080 --> 00:28:02.020
I'm not spelling that every single time.
我可不想每次都把那个词拼出来。

712
00:28:05.900 --> 00:28:10.060
This is, like, how strongly I felt about pockets in women's clothing.
这就是我对女性服装口袋问题的执念有多深。

713
00:28:10.980 --> 00:28:13.360
This is your soapbox moment, Angela.
这是你的个人演说时间，安吉拉。

714
00:28:13.820 --> 00:28:14.160
Yeah.
是啊。

715
00:28:14.160 --> 00:28:17.680
I can't tell you, like, how many times I've had to spell my street name out.
我简直没法告诉你，我不得不拼写我住的街道名字多少次了。

716
00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:18.340
It's annoying.
真的很烦人。

717
00:28:18.840 --> 00:28:19.980
Not going to say it.
我才不会说出来。

718
00:28:20.440 --> 00:28:21.680
Don't need the creepers.
不需要那些变态。

719
00:28:24.100 --> 00:28:25.780
You don't want anyone in your bush.
你不想让任何人进你的灌木丛。

720
00:28:25.960 --> 00:28:26.600
I don't want anyone.
我不想让任何人进。

721
00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:30.600
Well, I might want someone in my bush, but I think he already lives with you.
好吧，我可能想让某人进我的灌木丛，但我觉得他已经跟你住在一起了。

722
00:28:30.800 --> 00:28:31.260
I think.
我想是吧。

723
00:28:31.700 --> 00:28:32.960
Oh, geez, Louise.
噢，天哪。

724
00:28:34.260 --> 00:28:39.020
Oh, my gosh.
噢，我的天。

725
00:28:39.220 --> 00:28:40.440
I don't know what's happening to us today.
我不知道我们今天是怎么了。

726
00:28:40.440 --> 00:28:41.200
I don't know what's going on.
我不知道发生了什么。

727
00:28:41.200 --> 00:28:43.160
Should I go to New York more or less?
我是该多去几次纽约，还是少去几次？

728
00:28:43.160 --> 00:28:43.880
I don't know.
我不知道。

729
00:28:44.360 --> 00:28:45.320
I don't know.
我不知道。

730
00:28:46.220 --> 00:28:47.340
Oh, my Lord.
噢，天呐。

731
00:28:47.640 --> 00:28:53.360
We had some more questions because Jim, during this talking head, he's showing us his parents' house.
我们还有些问题，因为吉姆在这次采访中，向我们展示了他父母的房子。

732
00:28:53.820 --> 00:29:01.340
And Sam K would like to know, please explain the clown picture in Jim's parents' house.
山姆·K想知道，请解释一下吉姆父母家里的那幅小丑画。

733
00:29:01.600 --> 00:29:02.420
Please explain.
请解释一下。

734
00:29:02.420 --> 00:29:03.040
Yeah.
是啊。

735
00:29:03.340 --> 00:29:05.760
In the script, it just says,
剧本里只是写着，

736
00:29:17.460 --> 00:29:26.960
Randy Cordray told me that that clown painting was provided, it was made original for us by one of Phil Shea's go-to artists.
兰迪·科德雷告诉我，那幅小丑画是菲尔·谢伊手下的御用画师专门为我们创作的。

737
00:29:26.960 --> 00:29:30.300
He did not have the artist's name in his files.
他的档案里没有那位画师的名字。

738
00:29:30.620 --> 00:29:32.720
So we'd like to put it out there.
所以我们想公开征集一下。

739
00:29:32.860 --> 00:29:40.340
If you are listening and you are the person who painted the clown painting, will you contact us on Office Ladies Pod?
如果你正在收听节目，而且你就是画那幅小丑画的人，请通过《办公室女士》播客联系我们。

740
00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:41.720
We want to know more.
我们想了解更多信息。

741
00:29:41.960 --> 00:29:42.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

742
00:29:43.020 --> 00:29:50.740
But Randy Cordray said that the artist actually provided them with multiple preliminary choices.
但兰迪·科德雷说，那位画师实际上提供了多个初步方案供他们选择。

743
00:29:51.180 --> 00:29:58.920
And that Mindy, Greg, Paul, and Jen all had to stand and look at multiple clown paintings.
明迪、格雷格、保罗和詹当时不得不站着观看多幅小丑画。

744
00:29:59.380 --> 00:30:01.180
And that's the one they chose.
而那幅就是他们选中的。

745
00:30:01.640 --> 00:30:03.040
That was their job that day.
那就是他们那天的工作。

746
00:30:03.240 --> 00:30:03.500
Yeah.
是啊。

747
00:30:03.800 --> 00:30:04.940
Pick the clown painting.
挑选小丑画。

748
00:30:05.180 --> 00:30:05.800
That was your day.
那就是你的一天。

749
00:30:06.020 --> 00:30:06.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

750
00:30:06.360 --> 00:30:07.520
I had to pick a clown painting.
我得去挑一幅小丑画。

751
00:30:07.820 --> 00:30:08.760
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

752
00:30:09.220 --> 00:30:14.620
It cracked me up that it was on the wall like that and that he couldn't remove it because I feel like that's such a dad move.
它就那样挂在墙上，而且他没法把它取下来，这让我觉得特别好笑，因为我觉得这简直是典型的老爸行为。

753
00:30:15.080 --> 00:30:19.400
You know, it's like that moment where your mom is like, that painting is always tilted.
你知道，就像你妈总会说那幅画总是歪的。

754
00:30:19.400 --> 00:30:20.380
It's always tilted.
总是歪的。

755
00:30:20.560 --> 00:30:25.140
And then your dad goes and super glues it to the wall because he's tired of it tilting.
然后你爸就直接用强力胶把它粘在墙上，因为他受够了它总是歪来歪去。

756
00:30:25.620 --> 00:30:26.860
It just made me laugh.
这真的把我逗乐了。

757
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:29.640
I want to know the story behind why they bolted it down.
我想知道他们把它锁死在墙上的背后故事。

758
00:30:29.940 --> 00:30:30.220
Yeah.
是啊。

759
00:30:30.280 --> 00:30:32.380
What is the story there?
那背后的故事是什么？

760
00:30:32.740 --> 00:30:33.640
There's a story.
肯定有个故事。

761
00:30:34.240 --> 00:30:35.620
We don't know what it is exactly.
我们不知道具体是什么。

762
00:30:35.660 --> 00:30:36.260
We don't know.
我们不知道。

763
00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:38.420
Well, now, guess what?
好吧，现在，你猜怎么着？

764
00:30:38.740 --> 00:30:42.180
Oscar and Andy discover a note on the microwave.
奥斯卡和安迪在微波炉上发现了一张字条。

765
00:30:42.560 --> 00:30:44.320
It's a very shaming note.
那是一张非常羞辱人的字条。

766
00:30:44.760 --> 00:30:45.780
It is.
确实是。

767
00:30:48.070 --> 00:30:51.670
They think that the note is worse than the mess.
他们觉得这张字条比弄脏微波炉的行为更糟糕。

768
00:30:52.090 --> 00:30:53.610
Angela likes the note.
安吉拉倒是挺喜欢这张字条的。

769
00:30:53.850 --> 00:30:54.550
She does.
她是挺喜欢的。

770
00:30:55.170 --> 00:31:00.090
Meredith thinks that the person who wrote the note is definitely rich and should get off their high horse.
梅雷迪思觉得写这张字条的人肯定很有钱，应该从高高在上的姿态下来。

771
00:31:00.090 --> 00:31:03.510
I love this moment with this note on the microwave.
我喜欢微波炉上这张字条的这个桥段。

772
00:31:03.890 --> 00:31:04.590
I do, too.
我也喜欢。

773
00:31:04.710 --> 00:31:05.490
It's so relatable.
太有共鸣了。

774
00:31:05.490 --> 00:31:15.670
If you have ever worked in an office, there is at least once in your time of working in that office, a note stuck to something about something that people are like, eh.
如果你在办公室工作过，在你工作的这段时间里，至少会有那么一次，你会看到某样东西上贴着一张字条，关于某件让大家觉得“呃”的事情。

775
00:31:15.670 --> 00:31:21.650
Yeah, and also the note where the person leaving the note has clearly reached their limit.
没错，而且写字条的那个人显然已经忍无可忍了。

776
00:31:22.070 --> 00:31:23.050
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

777
00:31:23.170 --> 00:31:24.350
They can't take it anymore.
他们受够了。

778
00:31:24.690 --> 00:31:28.750
No, the note is masking a deep, like, river of anger.
不，这张字条掩盖了内心深处像河流一样汹涌的愤怒。

779
00:31:29.230 --> 00:31:29.330
Yeah.
是啊。

780
00:31:29.790 --> 00:31:31.010
They're just pissed.
他们只是气疯了。

781
00:31:31.710 --> 00:31:38.350
Well, I think this is such a fun moment because we get to see Pam and Angela in agreement about something.
我觉得这是一个非常有趣的时刻，因为我们看到帕姆和安吉拉在某件事上达成了共识。

782
00:31:38.730 --> 00:31:44.650
I think Pam starts to doubt her note a little bit when she realizes that Angela is on her side.
我觉得帕姆意识到安吉拉站在她这边时，开始对自己写的字条有点怀疑了。

783
00:31:44.770 --> 00:31:45.170
Do you think?
你觉得吗？

784
00:31:45.810 --> 00:31:47.110
Yeah, I do.
是的，我觉得。

785
00:31:47.830 --> 00:31:52.210
Well, the cool thing is that this moment at the microwave would have continued.
有趣的是，微波炉前的这个片段本可以继续下去的。

786
00:31:52.650 --> 00:31:58.130
In the script, there are two talking heads here, one from Pam and one from Angela.
在剧本里，这里有两个采访镜头，一个是帕姆的，一个是安吉拉的。

787
00:31:58.490 --> 00:31:58.830
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

788
00:31:59.070 --> 00:32:01.030
And, lady, I thought we could read them.
女士，我想我们可以读读看。

789
00:32:01.210 --> 00:32:01.950
I did, too.
我也这么想。

790
00:32:01.950 --> 00:32:03.830
And they really further the story.
它们确实推进了故事的发展。

791
00:32:03.830 --> 00:32:04.790
It's so fun.
太有趣了。

792
00:32:05.090 --> 00:32:07.490
Okay, here was Pam's talking head from the script.
好的，这是剧本里帕姆的采访镜头。

793
00:32:07.950 --> 00:32:09.330
She's holding up the note.
她举着那张字条。

794
00:32:09.890 --> 00:32:11.650
This is the front of the note.
这是字条的正面。

795
00:32:11.890 --> 00:32:13.810
And then it says, Pam holds up a memo.
然后上面写着，帕姆举起一张备忘录。

796
00:32:14.390 --> 00:32:17.390
This is the front of my latest office memorandum.
这是我最新办公室备忘录的正面。

797
00:32:17.630 --> 00:32:22.510
This can only lead anyone to believe that I wrote the note, which I did.
这只会让任何人相信是我写的字条，确实也是我写的。

798
00:32:22.790 --> 00:32:26.110
And then immediately it would cut to Angela's talking head.
然后紧接着会切到安吉拉的采访镜头。

799
00:32:26.250 --> 00:32:27.710
And this was what was in the script.
这就是剧本里的内容。

800
00:32:28.190 --> 00:32:31.630
Everyone keeps asking if I wrote the note on the microwave.
每个人都在问我是不是我写了微波炉上的那张字条。

801
00:32:32.010 --> 00:32:35.490
It was so perfectly worded and a little bit snotty.
措辞太完美了，还有点傲慢。

802
00:32:37.260 --> 00:32:38.640
I wish I had written it.
真希望那是我写的。

803
00:32:40.420 --> 00:32:45.880
Now, there were even more candy bag talking heads, which we'd filmed as well.
现在，还有更多关于糖果袋的采访镜头，我们也拍了。

804
00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:48.200
And they ended up in deleted scenes.
但最后都被剪掉了。

805
00:32:48.580 --> 00:32:50.420
But these are the two that were in the script.
不过这两个是剧本里有的。

806
00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:51.260
Yes.
是的。

807
00:32:51.480 --> 00:32:55.320
And you guys, what cracks me up as well, I don't know if you noticed this.
还有你们，让我觉得好笑的是，不知道你们有没有注意到。

808
00:32:55.720 --> 00:32:59.460
Not only are Pam and Angela kind of oddly on the same side of this argument.
帕姆和安吉拉不仅在这场争论中莫名其妙地站在了同一边。

809
00:32:59.660 --> 00:33:02.320
Did you notice, Jenna, that they're dressed alike?
珍娜，你注意到她们穿得一模一样了吗？

810
00:33:02.320 --> 00:33:03.280
Yes.
注意到了。

811
00:33:03.560 --> 00:33:08.520
I noticed that Pam is doing that thing that Angela always does where she wears like a weird
我注意到帕姆在做安吉拉常做的那种打扮，就是穿一件奇怪的

812
00:33:08.520 --> 00:33:10.880
short-sleeved sweater over a blouse.
短袖毛衣套在衬衫外面。

813
00:33:11.480 --> 00:33:17.260
They both have V-neck short-sleeved sweaters over short-sleeved blouses.
她们都穿着短袖V领毛衣，里面套着短袖衬衫。

814
00:33:17.700 --> 00:33:22.200
Angela's is like brown on brown and Pam's is black over purple.
安吉拉的是棕色配棕色，帕姆的是黑色配紫色。

815
00:33:22.440 --> 00:33:25.140
But what is this short-sleeved sweater?
但这种短袖毛衣到底是什么鬼？

816
00:33:25.140 --> 00:33:30.460
I have to believe that was a genius wardrobe choice by Alicia Raycraft.
我敢说这是艾丽西亚·雷克拉夫特天才般的服装选择。

817
00:33:30.700 --> 00:33:31.560
I think so.
我也这么觉得。

818
00:33:31.740 --> 00:33:33.140
Because that is funny.
因为这太搞笑了。

819
00:33:33.440 --> 00:33:34.500
I screen grabbed them.
我截了图。

