然后他接着说他感觉自己就像《惊声尖叫2》里的内芙·坎贝尔。

984
00:40:21.570 --> 00:40:25.730
And he has this very funny talking head where he learned a lot, I guess, from the Scream movies.
他有一个非常有趣的访谈镜头，我想他从《惊声尖叫》系列电影里学到了很多。

985
00:40:26.270 --> 00:40:29.570
But Jenna, there was another talking head in the script.
但是珍娜，剧本里还有另一个访谈镜头。

986
00:40:29.850 --> 00:40:32.130
So the one you see with the Neve Campbell.
就是你看到的那个关于内芙·坎贝尔的。

987
00:40:32.490 --> 00:40:32.650
Yep.
没错。

988
00:40:32.870 --> 00:40:34.010
That was not in the script.
那个不在剧本里。

989
00:40:34.010 --> 00:40:37.490
So that must have been an alternate talking head they handed him on the day.
所以那一定是他们当天临时给他的备选访谈镜头。

990
00:40:38.530 --> 00:40:41.030
In the script, this is Michael's talking head.
在剧本里，这是迈克尔的访谈镜头。

991
00:40:41.150 --> 00:40:43.770
It's almost the same right up until the evil snail.
除了“邪恶蜗牛”之外，几乎是一样的。

992
00:40:44.070 --> 00:40:46.230
So evil snail was in the script.
所以“邪恶蜗牛”是在剧本里的。

993
00:40:46.650 --> 00:40:47.150
Yes.
是的。

994
00:40:47.290 --> 00:40:48.770
Evil snail was a keeper.
“邪恶蜗牛”被保留了下来。

995
00:40:49.050 --> 00:40:50.190
We've always had that.
我们一直都有这个。

996
00:40:50.370 --> 00:40:52.470
But this is how it changed in the script.
但剧本里原本是这样写的。

997
00:40:52.670 --> 00:40:56.350
The last four months without Toby have been absolute bliss.
没有托比的这四个月简直是极乐世界。

998
00:40:56.670 --> 00:40:58.890
I fell in love with a beautiful blonde woman.
我爱上了一位美丽的金发女郎。

999
00:40:59.050 --> 00:41:00.230
I fell out of love.
我又失恋了。

1000
00:41:00.390 --> 00:41:01.370
I tried scallops.
我尝试了扇贝。

1001
00:41:01.530 --> 00:41:02.950
The office was broken into.
办公室被闯入了。

1002
00:41:03.170 --> 00:41:03.950
I became a father.
我当爸爸了。

1003
00:41:04.010 --> 00:41:05.050
I grew a goatee.
我留了山羊胡。

1004
00:41:05.190 --> 00:41:07.450
The Olympics were a great success for China.
北京奥运会取得了巨大成功。

1005
00:41:07.530 --> 00:41:10.330
And now that I've tasted freedom, I can never go back.
既然我已经尝到了自由的滋味，就再也回不去了。

1006
00:41:10.570 --> 00:41:11.850
I'm going to kill him.
我要杀了他。

1007
00:41:12.210 --> 00:41:13.030
No, too far.
不，太过分了。

1008
00:41:13.170 --> 00:41:14.210
But I will do something.
但我得做点什么。

1009
00:41:14.370 --> 00:41:14.870
No, too little.
不，这还不够。

1010
00:41:15.030 --> 00:41:15.990
I will get rid of him.
我要除掉他。

1011
00:41:16.250 --> 00:41:17.370
Oh, I like it.
哦，我喜欢这个主意。

1012
00:41:17.570 --> 00:41:19.710
I love his breakdown of what all happened.
我很喜欢他对所发生一切的梳理。

1013
00:41:19.870 --> 00:41:22.050
And I love that he included he grew a goatee.
而且我喜欢他把留山羊胡也写了进去。

1014
00:41:24.590 --> 00:41:25.290
Me too.
我也是。

1015
00:41:25.930 --> 00:41:30.810
It's true, in fact, that Michael is going to try to get rid of Toby.
事实上，迈克尔确实打算除掉托比。

1016
00:41:30.810 --> 00:41:33.710
He is looking for fireable offenses.
他在寻找能开除他的理由。

1017
00:41:34.270 --> 00:41:40.310
Dwight says there are two that he can find in this binder, workplace violence or sexual harassment.
德怀特说他在这个活页夹里找到了两条，职场暴力或性骚扰。

1018
00:41:40.310 --> 00:41:46.410
So I guess Michael's first plan is to try to get Toby to sexually harass Pam.
所以我猜迈克尔的第一个计划是想让托比去性骚扰帕姆。

1019
00:41:46.770 --> 00:41:48.490
He goes up to Pam's desk.
他走到帕姆的办公桌前。

1020
00:41:48.690 --> 00:41:50.150
He hands Pam a note.
他递给帕姆一张纸条。

1021
00:41:50.390 --> 00:41:53.290
And he says, go give this note to Toby.
他说，去把这张纸条交给托比。

1022
00:41:53.510 --> 00:41:54.150
Don't read it.
别看。

1023
00:41:54.350 --> 00:41:54.990
Don't read it.
别看。

1024
00:41:55.550 --> 00:41:56.690
Pam reads it.
帕姆看了。

1025
00:41:57.670 --> 00:42:00.710
In the note, it's written as if it's from Pam.
纸条上写的内容，看起来像是帕姆写的。

1026
00:42:00.950 --> 00:42:04.490
And it says, please hug and kiss me no matter how much I struggle.
上面写着，请拥抱并亲吻我，无论我怎么挣扎。

1027
00:42:04.730 --> 00:42:06.750
I'm too shy to confess my love to you.
我太害羞了，不敢向你表白。

1028
00:42:07.170 --> 00:42:09.910
Can you imagine if Toby had read that note?
你能想象如果托比读了那张纸条会怎样吗？

1029
00:42:10.290 --> 00:42:11.750
His brain would have exploded.
他的大脑会爆炸的。

1030
00:42:12.310 --> 00:42:12.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1031
00:42:13.090 --> 00:42:13.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1032
00:42:13.730 --> 00:42:15.030
Well, that doesn't work.
好吧，那招没用。

1033
00:42:15.470 --> 00:42:15.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1034
00:42:15.930 --> 00:42:18.110
Pam's like, no, I'm not going back there.
帕姆说，不，我才不去那儿。

1035
00:42:18.350 --> 00:42:24.110
So now the new plan is to get Toby to beat up Michael.
所以现在的新计划是让托比揍迈克尔。

1036
00:42:24.110 --> 00:42:30.690
Yeah, so they march back to the annex and Michael's sort of confronting Toby and trying to sort
是啊，于是他们大步走回隔间，迈克尔在那儿质问托比，试图……

1037
00:42:30.690 --> 00:42:32.610
of, you know, antagonize him to hit him.
你知道的，激怒他让他动手打人。

1038
00:42:32.730 --> 00:42:33.670
And Dwight's like, hit him.
德怀特在一旁喊，打他。

1039
00:42:33.790 --> 00:42:35.550
And then Kelly jumps in so quickly.
然后凯莉很快就插了进来。

1040
00:42:35.710 --> 00:42:36.230
Hit him.
打他。

1041
00:42:36.450 --> 00:42:37.030
I know.
我知道。

1042
00:42:37.170 --> 00:42:39.090
First of all, her and Ryan were making out.
首先，她和瑞安当时正在亲热。

1043
00:42:39.470 --> 00:42:39.890
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1044
00:42:40.030 --> 00:42:42.870
That they've stopped making out so that they can weigh in.
他们停下亲热，好发表一下意见。

1045
00:42:42.990 --> 00:42:44.310
And they're for a fight.
他们支持打架。

1046
00:42:44.490 --> 00:42:45.390
They're like, do it.
他们在那喊，动手啊。

1047
00:42:45.650 --> 00:42:46.150
Hit him.
打他。

1048
00:42:46.410 --> 00:42:46.850
Hit him.
打他。

1049
00:42:47.430 --> 00:42:48.150
Toby refuses.
托比拒绝了。

1050
00:42:48.710 --> 00:42:49.630
It's not working.
这招也不管用。

1051
00:42:50.190 --> 00:42:51.430
None of these plans are working.
这些计划都没用。

1052
00:42:51.930 --> 00:42:53.590
So you know what they're going to have to do.
所以你知道他们接下来得做什么了。

1053
00:42:54.110 --> 00:42:55.210
They're going to have to go big.
他们得搞点大的。

1054
00:42:55.390 --> 00:43:00.030
They're going to have to frame Toby for drugs, like on The Shield.
他们得像《盾牌》里那样，栽赃托比吸毒。

1055
00:43:00.410 --> 00:43:02.970
I love that Dwight said, I've framed many animals.
我太喜欢德怀特说的那句“我栽赃过很多动物”了。

1056
00:43:04.330 --> 00:43:06.910
I framed a raccoon opening a Christmas gift.
我栽赃过一只正在拆圣诞礼物的浣熊。

1057
00:43:07.790 --> 00:43:08.810
Oh, Dwight.
噢，德怀特。

1058
00:43:09.430 --> 00:43:14.930
Well, Michael thinks it sounds mean, but sometimes the end justifies the mean.
迈克尔觉得这听起来很刻薄，但有时为了目的可以不择手段。

1059
00:43:15.190 --> 00:43:16.390
That's such a good line.
那真是句好台词。

1060
00:43:16.610 --> 00:43:17.630
It's such a good line.
那真是句好台词。

1061
00:43:17.730 --> 00:43:18.910
It's so smart.
太聪明了。

1062
00:43:19.130 --> 00:43:20.310
It's smart funny.
既聪明又幽默。

1063
00:43:20.310 --> 00:43:23.050
It reminds me of this gem.
这让我想起了这句名言。

1064
00:43:23.350 --> 00:43:26.310
I'm not superstitious, but I'm a little bit stitious.
我不迷信，但我有点迷信。

1065
00:43:26.650 --> 00:43:27.110
Yes.
没错。

1066
00:43:27.450 --> 00:43:29.490
That it's right in line with that.
这和那句名言如出一辙。

1067
00:43:29.750 --> 00:43:35.610
So, yeah, Michael's going to go and hit up Leo and Gino over in Vance Refrigeration for
所以，迈克尔打算去找万斯制冷公司的里奥和吉诺，

1068
00:43:35.610 --> 00:43:36.290
some drugs.
搞点毒品。

1069
00:43:36.650 --> 00:43:40.890
They give him what they say is two pounds of weed and they want $500.
他们给了他两磅所谓的“大麻”，并索要500美元。

1070
00:43:41.650 --> 00:43:44.530
Michael has $500 in his wallet?
迈克尔钱包里有500美元？

1071
00:43:44.530 --> 00:43:46.470
I thought the same thing.
我也这么想。

1072
00:43:46.750 --> 00:43:48.830
That's a lot of cash in your wallet.
钱包里带那么多现金可不少见。

1073
00:43:49.090 --> 00:43:53.990
And for my background catch people, did you see the Lackawanna library card?
还有，给那些关注背景细节的朋友们，你们看到那张拉克瓦纳图书馆的借书证了吗？

1074
00:43:54.370 --> 00:43:55.710
In Michael's wallet?
在迈克尔的钱包里？

1075
00:43:56.010 --> 00:43:56.530
Yes.
是的。

1076
00:43:56.650 --> 00:44:00.610
When he opens his wallet, there's a Lackawanna County library card.
当他打开钱包时，里面有一张拉克瓦纳县的图书馆借书证。

1077
00:44:00.830 --> 00:44:03.790
Do you know what I found recently when I was cleaning out my closet?
你们知道我最近清理壁橱时发现了什么吗？

1078
00:44:04.130 --> 00:44:04.650
What?
什么？

1079
00:44:04.910 --> 00:44:05.910
Pam's wallet.
帕姆的钱包。

1080
00:44:06.210 --> 00:44:07.030
You did?
真的吗？

1081
00:44:07.030 --> 00:44:11.850
And in it, there's a credit card that says Pam Beasley.
里面有一张写着帕姆·比斯利的信用卡。

1082
00:44:12.170 --> 00:44:16.550
There's all these cards they made for my wallet, my prop wallet.
他们为我的钱包，也就是道具钱包，制作了所有这些卡片。

1083
00:44:16.750 --> 00:44:17.630
I'll take a picture.
我会拍张照片。

1084
00:44:17.750 --> 00:44:18.650
We'll put it in pod.
我们把它放到播客里。

1085
00:44:18.910 --> 00:44:20.290
Yeah, we have to put it in stories.
对，我们得把它发到快拍里。

1086
00:44:20.310 --> 00:44:21.330
That's so fun.
太有趣了。

1087
00:44:21.490 --> 00:44:22.610
How crazy is that?
这有多疯狂？

1088
00:44:22.750 --> 00:44:23.350
They did that.
他们竟然真的做了。

1089
00:44:23.470 --> 00:44:25.670
That's how detailed Phil Shea was.
这就是菲尔·谢伊的细节控程度。

1090
00:44:25.850 --> 00:44:25.970
Yep.
没错。

1091
00:44:26.190 --> 00:44:29.490
If you had a prop wallet, it reflected your character.
如果你有一个道具钱包，它会反映出你的角色特征。

1092
00:44:29.970 --> 00:44:33.330
Although, is Michael going to the library and why?
不过，迈克尔会去图书馆吗？为什么？

1093
00:44:33.490 --> 00:44:34.270
What's that for?
那是用来干嘛的？

1094
00:44:34.270 --> 00:44:40.290
I mean, I feel like Michael's probably had that library card for like 20 years in his wallet.
我是说，我觉得迈克尔可能在钱包里放那张借书证有20年了。

1095
00:44:41.310 --> 00:44:44.730
Maybe there was a time where he didn't have internet and he'd have to go to the library.
也许曾经有一段时间他没有网络，不得不去图书馆。

1096
00:44:44.990 --> 00:44:46.470
Oh, wait, we didn't have internet.
噢，等等，我们那时确实没有网络。

1097
00:44:47.390 --> 00:44:48.130
I know.
我知道。

1098
00:44:48.470 --> 00:44:53.270
Maybe he used to go to the library to make copies because the copier in the office is crap.
也许他以前常去图书馆复印文件，因为办公室的复印机太烂了。

1099
00:44:53.490 --> 00:44:54.950
We'll get to that next week.
我们下周再聊这个。

1100
00:44:55.370 --> 00:44:55.730
Yeah.
好的。

1101
00:44:56.350 --> 00:45:00.850
So, Ange, you know how when sometimes we're watching an episode or we're breaking down
安吉，你知道我们有时在看剧或者为了准备播客梳理文档时，

1102
00:45:00.850 --> 00:45:06.510
our document to prep to do the podcast, we'll get curious about something and we'll do a deep dive.
会对某件事产生好奇，然后进行深入研究。

1103
00:45:06.730 --> 00:45:08.050
Did you do one on something?
你这次有去研究什么吗？

1104
00:45:08.310 --> 00:45:09.310
I didn't.
我没有。

1105
00:45:09.470 --> 00:45:11.570
Our associate producer, Ainsley.
是我们的助理制片人安斯利。

1106
00:45:12.030 --> 00:45:13.430
Ainsley, what'd you deep dive?
安斯利，你深入研究了什么？

1107
00:45:14.510 --> 00:45:16.010
This is what she wrote me.
这是她写给我的。

1108
00:45:16.010 --> 00:45:23.190
She said, according to a regrettable Google search, the price of one pound of recreational
她说，根据一次令人遗憾的谷歌搜索，在宾夕法尼亚州，一磅娱乐用

1109
00:45:23.190 --> 00:45:29.910
marijuana in Pennsylvania ranges from $1,900 to $2,550.
大麻的价格在1900美元到2550美元之间。

1110
00:45:30.630 --> 00:45:31.950
She had to know.
她非得弄清楚不可。

1111
00:45:32.110 --> 00:45:36.090
She was like, okay, they're selling Michael two pounds of weed for $500.
她当时想，好吧，他们以500美元的价格卖给迈克尔两磅大麻。

1112
00:45:36.910 --> 00:45:37.970
Ainsley got curious.
安斯利好奇了。

1113
00:45:37.970 --> 00:45:41.090
How much is a pound of weed in Pennsylvania?
在宾夕法尼亚州，一磅大麻要多少钱？

1114
00:45:41.090 --> 00:45:44.990
And now I looked and we shot this in September of 2008.
我查了一下，我们是在2008年9月拍摄这一集的。

1115
00:45:44.990 --> 00:45:47.190
So how much was it in 2008?
那么在2008年是多少钱呢？

1116
00:45:47.490 --> 00:45:51.990
I'm not sure, but today that's going to run you quite a bit of money.
我不确定，但以现在的价格，那可要花不少钱。

1117
00:45:52.490 --> 00:45:58.410
With today's prices, Michael got a deal because it would cost him close to $5,000 to get two
按今天的价格，迈克尔算是捡到便宜了，因为买两磅大麻

1118
00:45:58.410 --> 00:45:59.590
pounds of weed today.
现在得花将近5000美元。

1119
00:45:59.910 --> 00:46:05.070
I also want to say that's clearly not two pounds of anything in that baggie.
我还想说，那个小袋子里装的显然不是两磅任何东西。

1120
00:46:05.370 --> 00:46:05.910
No.
没错。

1121
00:46:06.270 --> 00:46:08.810
It's green, but it's not two pounds.
那是绿色的，但绝对不到两磅。

1122
00:46:08.810 --> 00:46:14.110
I mean, two pounds, I have two pounds of things all over my house, like two pound weights,
我是说，两磅，我家里到处都是两磅重的东西，比如两磅重的哑铃，

1123
00:46:14.350 --> 00:46:15.390
two pound bag of flour.
两磅重的面粉袋。

1124
00:46:15.610 --> 00:46:17.690
That's not two pounds of anything.
那袋子里装的根本不是两磅重的东西。

1125
00:46:18.330 --> 00:46:19.110
It's not.
确实不是。

1126
00:46:19.310 --> 00:46:22.070
I've had a two pound bag of spinach in my house before.
我以前买过两磅重的菠菜。

1127
00:46:22.290 --> 00:46:23.410
It's much bigger than that.
比那个大多了。

1128
00:46:23.490 --> 00:46:24.890
It takes up the whole crisper drawer.
能把整个保鲜抽屉都塞满。

1129
00:46:25.130 --> 00:46:30.470
You're very passionate about painting a very clear picture of what two pounds is.
你对于描绘两磅到底有多重这件事真是充满热情。

1130
00:46:30.650 --> 00:46:34.550
I mean, it's so glaringly obvious that that's not two pounds.
我是说，那袋子明显不是两磅，这太显而易见了。

1131
00:46:34.690 --> 00:46:36.990
There are so many signs that Michael is missing.
迈克尔错过了太多迹象。

1132
00:46:37.250 --> 00:46:38.610
Don't get Jenna started.
别让珍娜开始唠叨这个。

1133
00:46:38.810 --> 00:46:41.990
Don't get me started on what two pounds of something is.
别让我开始唠叨两磅到底是多少。

1134
00:46:42.190 --> 00:46:44.570
I'll tell you about my two pounds of spinach.
我可以跟你讲讲我的两磅菠菜。

1135
00:46:44.890 --> 00:46:49.850
I just ordered two pounds of Epsom salts, and that was a large package as well.
我刚订了两磅泻盐，那也是一大包。

1136
00:46:50.170 --> 00:46:51.110
What are you making?
你要做什么？

1137
00:46:51.370 --> 00:46:52.710
Warm, soothing bath.
泡个温暖舒适的澡。

1138
00:46:54.950 --> 00:46:59.930
Well, listen, we're about to find out that Pam has an ally in this whole microwave business.
好吧，听着，我们马上就会发现帕姆在微波炉这件事上有一个盟友。

1139
00:47:00.530 --> 00:47:01.270
Does she?
是吗？

1140
00:47:01.450 --> 00:47:06.630
She has Ryan, who's pretending to be an ally, and he's laying it on thick, and I love it.
她有瑞安，他假装是盟友，而且演得非常卖力，我喜欢。

1141
00:47:07.110 --> 00:47:09.130
Yeah, he says, I'm totally on your side.
是啊，他说，我完全站在你这边。

1142
00:47:09.130 --> 00:47:13.230
But the truth is, he went to make a cup of noodles, and the microwave is still a mess.
但事实是，他去泡杯面，发现微波炉还是乱七八糟的。

1143
00:47:13.370 --> 00:47:14.790
And he wants her to clean it up.
他想让帕姆去清理。

1144
00:47:14.870 --> 00:47:17.410
And she delivers some real Pam sass.
而帕姆展现了她真正的毒舌。

1145
00:47:18.150 --> 00:47:18.710
Hey, Pam.
嘿，帕姆。

1146
00:47:19.370 --> 00:47:23.550
I just want to let you know, I'm totally on your side with the whole microwave situation.
我只是想让你知道，关于微波炉的情况，我完全站在你这边。

1147
00:47:24.510 --> 00:47:25.150
Thank you.
谢谢。

1148
00:47:25.330 --> 00:47:27.230
I was just back there to make some cup of soup.
我刚才去后面泡杯汤。

1149
00:47:27.370 --> 00:47:28.690
The thing is still a huge mess.
那玩意儿还是乱得一塌糊涂。

1150
00:47:28.850 --> 00:47:29.110
I know.
我知道。

1151
00:47:29.210 --> 00:47:29.830
Can you believe it?
你敢相信吗？

1152
00:47:29.970 --> 00:47:30.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1153
00:47:30.510 --> 00:47:31.170
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

1154
00:47:32.210 --> 00:47:38.830
But I guess the thing is, at some point, notes or no notes, someone's going to have to just get in there and clean it up.
但我猜重点是，不管有没有纸条，总得有人进去把它清理干净。

1155
00:47:40.910 --> 00:47:42.630
I guess that's why we have a temp, huh?
我想这就是为什么我们要请临时工，对吧？

1156
00:47:45.150 --> 00:47:45.770
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1157
00:47:46.090 --> 00:47:46.430
Trust me.
相信我。

1158
00:47:46.530 --> 00:47:47.730
I would just make it worse.
我只会越弄越糟。

1159
00:47:47.970 --> 00:47:49.870
How would wiping it with a paper towel make it worse?
用纸巾擦一下怎么会越弄越糟呢？

1160
00:47:49.930 --> 00:47:50.830
I would find a way.
我总能找到办法的。

1161
00:47:51.650 --> 00:47:53.290
You've seen things clean before, though, right?
但你以前见过东西被清理干净的样子吧？

1162
00:47:53.670 --> 00:47:55.250
Pam, I'm hopeless to that stuff.
帕姆，我对那种事一窍不通。

1163
00:47:56.530 --> 00:47:59.810
I mean, that's some good Pam sass.
我是说，那真是帕姆式的毒舌。

1164
00:47:59.990 --> 00:48:01.090
That was all scripted.
那全是照着剧本演的。

1165
00:48:01.230 --> 00:48:03.250
I know it sounds like Jenna sass.
我知道听起来像珍娜的毒舌。

1166
00:48:03.410 --> 00:48:04.310
It was scripted.
那是剧本写的。

1167
00:48:04.450 --> 00:48:06.090
I just brought myself to it.
我只是带入了真情实感。

1168
00:48:06.230 --> 00:48:07.950
You brought some real truth to it.
你确实带入了真实的感受。

1169
00:48:08.010 --> 00:48:08.390
I did.
我确实带入了。

1170
00:48:09.030 --> 00:48:14.870
Well, Ange, we got a lot of fan questions asking, who did clean the microwave?
好吧，安吉，我们收到很多粉丝提问，到底是谁清理了微波炉？

1171
00:48:15.330 --> 00:48:17.290
Because this never gets wrapped up.
因为这事儿从来没交代过。

1172
00:48:17.430 --> 00:48:18.450
We never find out.
我们永远没查出来。

1173
00:48:18.650 --> 00:48:19.710
Did it get clean?
它被清理了吗？

1174
00:48:19.810 --> 00:48:20.490
Who cleaned it?
谁清理的？

1175
00:48:20.750 --> 00:48:22.570
This would have wrapped up.
这本来是可以交代清楚的。

1176
00:48:22.670 --> 00:48:23.730
It's in the script.
剧本里有写。

1177
00:48:23.930 --> 00:48:26.830
And we filmed a big scene that would have explained all of it.
而且我们拍了一场大戏，本来可以解释这一切的。

1178
00:48:27.010 --> 00:48:28.630
It was a fun scene, too.
那也是一场很有趣的戏。

1179
00:48:29.070 --> 00:48:29.770
It was.
确实。

1180
00:48:29.770 --> 00:48:32.930
And it has a great Pam Angela moment at the top.
而且开头有一个很棒的帕姆和安吉的互动时刻。

1181
00:48:33.170 --> 00:48:33.510
Yeah.
是啊。

1182
00:48:33.830 --> 00:48:35.290
So it starts with Angela.
故事是从安吉拉开始的。

1183
00:48:35.490 --> 00:48:36.890
She's storming in from the kitchen.
她从厨房气冲冲地走进来。

1184
00:48:36.890 --> 00:48:38.590
And she's super ticked off.
她超级生气。

1185
00:48:38.690 --> 00:48:40.130
And she's holding up a note.
手里还举着一张纸条。

1186
00:48:40.430 --> 00:48:43.870
Someone has drawn a penis on the note.
有人在纸条上画了个丁丁。

1187
00:48:43.870 --> 00:48:45.050
And she confronts Pam.
然后她去质问帕姆。

1188
00:48:45.410 --> 00:48:45.810
I know.
我知道。

1189
00:48:45.890 --> 00:48:47.530
She thinks Pam drew the penis.
她以为是帕姆画的。

1190
00:48:48.230 --> 00:48:51.710
Why does she always blame Pam for this kind of stuff?
为什么她总是把这种事怪到帕姆头上？

1191
00:48:51.850 --> 00:48:52.630
I don't know.
我不知道。

1192
00:48:52.870 --> 00:48:53.770
Here's how it went.
当时的情况是这样的。

1193
00:48:55.010 --> 00:48:55.510
Pervert.
变态。

1194
00:48:57.070 --> 00:48:58.330
Angela, I didn't do that.
安吉拉，那不是我画的。

1195
00:48:58.330 --> 00:49:00.750
So is this what they taught you at your fancy art school?
这就是你在那所高级艺术学校学到的东西吗？

1196
00:49:00.910 --> 00:49:02.490
Why would I draw a penis on my own note?
我为什么要在我自己的纸条上画丁丁？

1197
00:49:02.850 --> 00:49:04.190
Why do you wear bright colors?
那你为什么要穿颜色鲜艳的衣服？

1198
00:49:04.430 --> 00:49:05.150
For attention, Pam.
为了博眼球，帕姆。

1199
00:49:07.590 --> 00:49:09.510
Everyone, I have an announcement to make.
各位，我有件事要宣布。

1200
00:49:11.350 --> 00:49:13.830
I'm the person who put the first note on the microwave.
我就是那个在微波炉上贴第一张纸条的人。

1201
00:49:15.210 --> 00:49:17.030
Yeah, Pam comes clean.
没错，帕姆坦白了。

1202
00:49:17.410 --> 00:49:22.590
And I remember shooting this because Pam kind of goes on to take charge of the room.
我记得拍这一幕的时候，帕姆开始掌控全场了。

1203
00:49:22.790 --> 00:49:27.870
After she admits that she wrote the note, she's like, and I guess I just have to say,
在她承认纸条是她写的时候，她就像是，我想我不得不说，

1204
00:49:28.010 --> 00:49:30.350
what's so wrong about the note?
那张纸条到底有什么问题？

1205
00:49:30.490 --> 00:49:33.250
Why is everyone so offended by this note?
为什么大家对这张纸条这么反感？

1206
00:49:33.450 --> 00:49:37.110
Shouldn't you be more offended by a consistently dirty microwave?
难道你们不该对那个一直脏兮兮的微波炉更反感吗？

1207
00:49:37.470 --> 00:49:39.130
She gets on her soapbox.
她开始发表长篇大论了。

1208
00:49:39.270 --> 00:49:40.490
It's Pam's soapbox.
这是帕姆的个人秀。

1209
00:49:40.490 --> 00:49:41.790
It's Pam's soapbox.
这是帕姆的个人秀。

1210
00:49:41.950 --> 00:49:47.170
And you guys, as an actor, when we got to have a moment where we commanded the whole bullpen,
伙计们，作为演员，当我们能有这样一个掌控整个办公室的时刻时，

1211
00:49:47.190 --> 00:49:48.470
it was exciting.
真的很令人兴奋。

1212
00:49:48.470 --> 00:49:50.610
And also we were like kind of terrified.
但同时我们也感到有点害怕。

1213
00:49:50.910 --> 00:49:51.470
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

1214
00:49:51.650 --> 00:49:53.630
Because you're in charge of like the pace of the scene.
因为你要掌控整场戏的节奏。

1215
00:49:53.810 --> 00:49:57.370
This only happened to me a handful of times when Angela makes a big announcement or something.
这种事我只经历过几次，通常是安吉拉宣布什么重大消息的时候。

1216
00:49:57.710 --> 00:50:01.890
But I remember, Jenna, watching you and you were so good in this moment because
但我记得，珍娜，看着你的时候，你在这场戏里表现得太棒了，因为

1217
00:50:01.890 --> 00:50:06.770
everyone is like throwing you little curveballs, you know, Oscar and Stanley and Kevin,
每个人都在给你出难题，你知道的，奥斯卡、斯坦利还有凯文，

1218
00:50:07.010 --> 00:50:08.730
you know, they're all kind of sassing you.
他们都在对你冷嘲热讽。

1219
00:50:08.730 --> 00:50:14.770
And, you know, the last time that I had a scene like this was back in Beach Games when Pam was
你知道，我上一次有这种戏份还是在“海滩游戏”那一集，当时帕姆

1220
00:50:14.770 --> 00:50:19.130
going to confront the whole group about her feelings and how they didn't come to her art
要向大家倾诉她的感受，抱怨他们没去参加她的艺术

1221
00:50:19.130 --> 00:50:19.450
show.
展。

1222
00:50:19.590 --> 00:50:23.190
But in this instance, people were interrupting me and they're coming at me.
但在这一幕里，大家不断打断我，还针对我。

1223
00:50:23.250 --> 00:50:27.830
And I got such a window into what Steve's every day was.
我终于窥见了一点史蒂夫每天的工作状态。

1224
00:50:28.790 --> 00:50:33.850
At one point, the group starts hazing Pam about being in New York.
有一刻，大家开始因为帕姆去过纽约而起哄。

1225
00:50:34.210 --> 00:50:37.830
And Pam gives this speech that kind of takes Jim off guard.
帕姆发表了一番让吉姆措手不及的演讲。

1226
00:50:37.910 --> 00:50:39.450
And I think we should hear it.
我觉得我们应该听听这段。

1227
00:50:40.150 --> 00:50:43.010
Listen, New York, that might fly.
听着，在纽约那一套或许行得通。

1228
00:50:43.210 --> 00:50:43.450
Why?
为什么？

1229
00:50:43.610 --> 00:50:45.270
Because I went to New York for three months.
因为我在纽约待了三个月。

1230
00:50:45.610 --> 00:50:47.430
That and the black sweater of Manhattan.
还有那件曼哈顿的黑色毛衣。

1231
00:50:47.890 --> 00:50:50.130
OK, yes, I went to New York, everybody.
好吧，没错，我去过纽约，各位。

1232
00:50:50.370 --> 00:50:51.970
I'm not going to apologize for it.
我不会为此道歉。

1233
00:50:51.970 --> 00:50:55.750
I experienced more there in one week than I experienced here in three months.
我在那里一周的经历比我在这里三个月的经历还要多。

1234
00:50:55.890 --> 00:50:56.790
I love New York.
我爱纽约。

1235
00:50:57.050 --> 00:50:59.890
You know, I especially love that people there cleaned up after themselves.
你知道，我特别喜欢那里的人会自己清理垃圾。

1236
00:51:00.330 --> 00:51:02.130
Well, Jim has just heard her say all that.
吉姆刚听完她说的这些话。

1237
00:51:02.450 --> 00:51:02.650
Yeah.
没错。

1238
00:51:02.810 --> 00:51:07.830
And the camera is pushing in on his face and he's realizing at the end of today, he's going
镜头推向他的脸，他意识到今天结束时，他要

1239
00:51:07.830 --> 00:51:10.490
to tell her he bought them a house in Scranton.
告诉她，他在斯克兰顿给他们买了栋房子。

1240
00:51:10.590 --> 00:51:12.790
She's not going back to New York anytime soon.
她短期内不会再回纽约了。

1241
00:51:12.950 --> 00:51:14.270
This place she loves.
这个她所热爱的地方。

1242
00:51:14.270 --> 00:51:18.790
I really wish this moment had made it into the show because I feel like it just sets
我真希望这一幕能保留在正片里，因为我觉得它为吉姆

1243
00:51:18.790 --> 00:51:23.450
up the stakes for Jim because he's doubting his decision from the very beginning.
设定了赌注，因为他从一开始就在怀疑自己的决定。

1244
00:51:23.630 --> 00:51:24.430
Did I do the right thing?
我做对了吗？

1245
00:51:24.490 --> 00:51:25.330
Is she going to like this?
她会喜欢吗？

1246
00:51:25.410 --> 00:51:25.930
I don't know.
我不知道。

1247
00:51:26.110 --> 00:51:28.010
And I feel like he needed to hear this.
我觉得他需要听到这些。

1248
00:51:28.090 --> 00:51:30.030
And I feel like the audience needed to hear it.
我也觉得观众需要听到这些。

1249
00:51:30.190 --> 00:51:30.610
I do, too.
我也是这么想的。

1250
00:51:30.670 --> 00:51:32.170
I think it's a shame that it got cut out.
我觉得被剪掉真是太可惜了。

1251
00:51:32.330 --> 00:51:37.950
And, you know, at the end of this whole scene, Pam says, fine, I'll go clean it.
而且，你知道，在整场戏的最后，帕姆说，好吧，我去把它清理干净。

1252
00:51:38.350 --> 00:51:42.110
So it is Pam in the end who cleaned the microwave.
所以最后确实是帕姆清理了微波炉。

1253
00:51:42.110 --> 00:51:49.370
Yes, in the script, the very last line of this big scene says this, Pam marches over to
是的，在剧本里，这场大戏的最后一句台词是这样写的，帕姆大步走向

1254
00:51:49.370 --> 00:51:53.090
the kitchen and Stanley starts to slow clap.
厨房，然后斯坦利开始缓慢地鼓掌。

1255
00:51:55.070 --> 00:51:55.590
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1256
00:51:56.110 --> 00:51:59.650
We had a slow clap that didn't make it.
我们拍了一段缓慢鼓掌的戏，但没用上。

1257
00:51:59.950 --> 00:52:01.290
Oh, yeah, that's right.
哦，对，没错。

1258
00:52:01.490 --> 00:52:05.170
Oh, that's bringing back that memory of me walking to Stanley's slow clap.
哦，那让我想起了我走过去时斯坦利缓慢鼓掌的画面。

1259
00:52:05.810 --> 00:52:06.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1260
00:52:07.570 --> 00:52:08.450
So good.
太棒了。

1261
00:52:08.870 --> 00:52:09.510
So good.
太棒了。

1262
00:52:10.150 --> 00:52:17.070
It's time for Michael to plant what he thinks is two pounds of marijuana in Toby's desk.
现在是迈克尔要把他以为是两磅大麻的东西放进托比办公桌的时候了。

1263
00:52:17.330 --> 00:52:23.550
And at the same time, Dwight is going to call the police and report that there is a drug
与此同时，德怀特要打电话给警察，举报说有一名毒贩

1264
00:52:23.550 --> 00:52:26.210
dealer named Toby Flunderson on the premises.
叫托比·弗兰德森的人在公司里。

1265
00:52:26.530 --> 00:52:30.150
And when asked to give his name, Dwight says his name is Andy Bernard.
当被要求报上名字时，德怀特说他的名字是安迪·伯纳德。

1266
00:52:30.490 --> 00:52:33.690
Dwight is going to throw Andy under the bus any chance he gets.
德怀特只要有机会就会把安迪推出去当替罪羊。

1267
00:52:33.690 --> 00:52:38.430
There was this deleted scene, Jenna, that for Michael to be able to have the time to go
珍娜，有一个删减片段，为了让迈克尔有时间去

1268
00:52:38.430 --> 00:52:41.830
plant the drugs, they needed to get Toby away from his desk.
藏毒品，他们需要把托比从办公桌旁支开。

1269
00:52:42.170 --> 00:52:46.210
So Dwight asked Toby to show him his photos from Costa Rica.
所以德怀特让托比给他看他在哥斯达黎加拍的照片。

1270
00:52:46.390 --> 00:52:47.650
Let's go to the conference room.
我们去会议室吧。

1271
00:52:47.850 --> 00:52:48.830
I'll look at your photos.
我会看看你的照片。

1272
00:52:49.210 --> 00:52:51.710
Toby is thrilled that someone wants to see his photos.
托比很高兴有人想看他的照片。

1273
00:52:52.090 --> 00:52:54.470
And then Michael sneaks off to plant the drugs.
然后迈克尔溜走去藏毒品。

1274
00:52:54.630 --> 00:52:58.690
But in true Michael fashion, he can't keep the secret.
但迈克尔的本性使然，他藏不住秘密。

1275
00:52:58.690 --> 00:53:02.130
He has to share with someone that he might have just done something.
他必须找个人分享他刚刚可能做了一件大事。

1276
00:53:02.130 --> 00:53:03.370
This is what he said.
这是他说的。

1277
00:53:03.890 --> 00:53:06.870
I think it's really cool that you wanted to see my photos.
我觉得你想看我的照片真的很酷。

1278
00:53:07.170 --> 00:53:08.950
What's this pink thing on that white oval?
那个白色椭圆形上的粉色东西是什么？

1279
00:53:09.090 --> 00:53:09.430
That's me.
那是我。

1280
00:53:09.570 --> 00:53:10.370
I was boogie boarding.
我在玩趴板冲浪。

1281
00:53:10.690 --> 00:53:12.630
Wait, who took this picture?
等等，这张照片是谁拍的？

1282
00:53:12.930 --> 00:53:13.790
Did you make some friends?
你交到朋友了吗？

1283
00:53:14.550 --> 00:53:19.230
Oh, I hired a local kid to snap it.
哦，我雇了个当地小孩帮我拍的。

1284
00:53:19.710 --> 00:53:20.590
Tell me about this monkey.
跟我说说这只猴子。

1285
00:53:23.450 --> 00:53:26.050
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

1286
00:53:26.670 --> 00:53:27.070
I'm not.
我不能。

1287
00:53:28.170 --> 00:53:30.110
I am not at liberty to talk about it.
我不方便谈论这件事。

1288
00:53:30.110 --> 00:53:35.250
Let's just say that I somethinged something in somebody something.
只能说我把某样东西在某人的某处做了某事。

1289
00:53:36.230 --> 00:53:39.030
And if discovered, then someone will get something.
如果被发现的话，那某人就会得到某种后果。

1290
00:53:40.210 --> 00:53:41.670
I may have said too much.
我可能说得太多了。

1291
00:53:41.970 --> 00:53:43.350
He can't not say anything.
他就是忍不住要说点什么。

1292
00:53:43.550 --> 00:53:44.030
He can't.
他忍不住。

1293
00:53:44.230 --> 00:53:46.070
Containment is not his strong suit.
克制不是他的强项。

1294
00:53:46.390 --> 00:53:46.630
No.
没错。

1295
00:53:47.010 --> 00:53:53.830
And then I have to say, that scene with Dwight and Toby, to me, it sounded like Rainn Wilson
而且我得说，德怀特和托比的那场戏，听起来就像雷恩·威尔森

1296
00:53:53.830 --> 00:53:57.070
improvising questions trying to stump Paul Lieberstein.
在即兴提问，试图难倒保罗·利伯斯坦。

1297
00:53:57.070 --> 00:53:58.610
Jenna, you're not wrong.
珍娜，你说得没错。

1298
00:53:58.810 --> 00:54:00.310
I'm looking at the script right now.
我现在正在看剧本。

1299
00:54:00.470 --> 00:54:04.830
The part with what's the red thing crawling on that oval, that was scripted.
关于那个椭圆形上爬着的红色东西是什么的部分，那是剧本里写的。

1300
00:54:04.950 --> 00:54:05.250
Okay.
好吧。

1301
00:54:05.610 --> 00:54:08.450
But the tell me about this monkey is not in the script.
但关于这只猴子的事剧本里没写啊。

1302
00:54:08.730 --> 00:54:09.050
Okay.
好吧。

1303
00:54:09.410 --> 00:54:11.950
Also, what about that question, who took these pictures?
还有，那个问题呢，到底是谁拍的这些照片？

1304
00:54:12.290 --> 00:54:13.110
That's in the script.
那在剧本里。

1305
00:54:13.310 --> 00:54:14.170
Oh, it is.
哦，是吗。

1306
00:54:14.350 --> 00:54:14.570
Yeah.
是的。

1307
00:54:14.570 --> 00:54:15.610
That's a funny line.
那句台词挺有意思的。

1308
00:54:15.850 --> 00:54:17.470
The improv moment is the monkey.
即兴发挥的部分是猴子。

1309
00:54:17.470 --> 00:54:18.030
Okay.
好吧。

1310
00:54:18.410 --> 00:54:24.270
Now the police arrive, and they are going to look into this possible narcotics situation.
现在警察到了，他们要调查这起疑似毒品案件。

1311
00:54:24.630 --> 00:54:26.330
Pam doesn't know anything about it.
帕姆对此一无所知。

1312
00:54:26.710 --> 00:54:27.890
Dwight's going to take charge.
德怀特打算接手负责。

1313
00:54:28.210 --> 00:54:30.210
And then Michael starts freaking out.
然后迈克尔开始抓狂了。

1314
00:54:30.370 --> 00:54:30.670
Yes.
没错。

1315
00:54:30.790 --> 00:54:34.130
And then they realize it's a Ziploc of maybe like, what, a caprese salad?
接着他们意识到那袋密封袋里装的可能是，怎么说呢，卡普里沙拉？

1316
00:54:34.450 --> 00:54:34.910
Yeah.
没错。

1317
00:54:35.050 --> 00:54:38.190
It looks like there's definitely some cheese in there.
看起来里面肯定有奶酪。

1318
00:54:38.490 --> 00:54:38.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1319
00:54:39.010 --> 00:54:40.330
And some salad dressing.
还有一些沙拉酱。

1320
00:54:41.010 --> 00:54:41.210
Yeah.
没错。

1321
00:54:41.210 --> 00:54:46.950
I'll have you know, the police officers were played by Patrick Fawcett and Michael Harity,
我得告诉你们，那两位警官是由帕特里克·福塞特和迈克尔·哈里蒂饰演的，

1322
00:54:47.150 --> 00:54:49.290
and neither of them have been on Monk.
他们俩都没演过《神探阿蒙》。

1323
00:54:49.470 --> 00:54:50.150
I checked.
我查过了。

1324
00:54:50.590 --> 00:54:52.310
Oh, good call to check, though.
哦，不过查一下确实是个好主意。

1325
00:54:52.830 --> 00:54:58.850
Also, can we talk about how when the police first arrived, Creed stood up as if he was
另外，我们能聊聊警察刚到时，克里德站起来好像要被戴上手铐一样吗？

1326
00:54:58.850 --> 00:54:59.850
going to be handcuffed?
然后把手放在脑后？

1327
00:55:00.010 --> 00:55:02.090
And then put his hands behind his head?
然后把手放在脑后？

1328
00:55:02.350 --> 00:55:02.590
Yeah.
没错。

1329
00:55:02.790 --> 00:55:07.170
And then his talking head where he's like, just keep talking to me until the police leave.
还有他的单人采访，他说，一直跟我说话直到警察离开。

1330
00:55:07.410 --> 00:55:08.090
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1331
00:55:08.350 --> 00:55:08.930
So good.
太棒了。

1332
00:55:09.070 --> 00:55:10.290
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

1333
00:55:10.290 --> 00:55:11.890
We got some fan mail.
我们收到了一些粉丝来信。

1334
00:55:12.070 --> 00:55:12.490
Brooke L.
布鲁克·L。

1335
00:55:12.710 --> 00:55:17.470
said that Toby seemed very concerned about police officers searching his desk.
说托比似乎非常担心警察搜查他的办公桌。

1336
00:55:17.870 --> 00:55:21.870
Could this be because they might find evidence of him being the Scranton Strangler?
这会不会是因为他们可能会发现他是“斯克兰顿勒杀手”的证据？

1337
00:55:22.270 --> 00:55:22.650
Oh.
哦。

1338
00:55:23.410 --> 00:55:24.250
I don't know.
我不知道。

1339
00:55:24.570 --> 00:55:31.910
At 16 minutes, 27 seconds, we have a very rare side-by-side talking head.
在16分27秒处，我们看到了一个非常罕见的并排单人采访。

1340
00:55:32.230 --> 00:55:33.030
So rare.
太罕见了。

1341
00:55:33.230 --> 00:55:34.370
How did they get through it?
他们是怎么拍完的？

1342
00:55:34.550 --> 00:55:35.410
I don't know.
我不知道。

1343
00:55:35.670 --> 00:55:37.850
Michael and Toby side-by-side.
迈克尔和托比并排坐着。

1344
00:55:38.030 --> 00:55:38.930
I know.
我知道。

1345
00:55:38.930 --> 00:55:42.390
I would have loved to have been a fly on a wall on that talking head because you know.
我真希望能在那场采访时做一只墙上的苍蝇，因为你知道的。

1346
00:55:42.590 --> 00:55:43.730
I looked for the bloopers.
我找了花絮。

1347
00:55:43.890 --> 00:55:47.110
I was like, surely, surely there's something on the blooper reel.
我在想，肯定，肯定会有什么花絮片段。

1348
00:55:47.610 --> 00:55:48.090
Yes.
是的。

1349
00:55:48.090 --> 00:55:48.530
Yes.
是的。

1350
00:55:48.670 --> 00:55:50.570
Because I was like, I know these guys.
因为我在想，我了解这些人。

1351
00:55:50.810 --> 00:55:52.290
I know Steve and Paul together.
我认识史蒂夫和保罗，他们俩关系很好。

1352
00:55:52.290 --> 00:55:57.690
And they were as tickled by the Toby-Michael relationship as the audience was, as we all
他们和观众一样，对托比和迈克尔那种关系感到忍俊不禁，我们大家也都一样。

1353
00:55:57.690 --> 00:55:58.050
were.
确实。

1354
00:55:58.290 --> 00:55:58.750
Yes.
没错。

1355
00:55:58.830 --> 00:56:00.290
And they would mess with each other.
而且他们还会互相捉弄。

1356
00:56:00.450 --> 00:56:04.930
You remember in a scene, there's a blooper where Toby has to hand Michael a piece of
你还记得有个场景吗，有个花絮是托比得递给迈克尔一张纸，

1357
00:56:04.930 --> 00:56:08.570
paper and Steve and him start cracking up because Paul wrote, f*** you on it?
结果史蒂夫和他都笑场了，因为保罗在纸上写了“去你的”？

1358
00:56:08.750 --> 00:56:09.130
Yes.
记得。

1359
00:56:10.310 --> 00:56:15.230
So I know they were giving it to each other, and I wish there were some bloopers from this.
所以我知道他们当时在互相开玩笑，我真希望这部分能有些花絮。

1360
00:56:15.330 --> 00:56:17.110
There is footage somewhere for sure.
肯定有录像存世的。

1361
00:56:17.670 --> 00:56:21.910
Well, listen, in the annex, Ryan and Kelly are making out again.
好了，听着，在办公区，瑞安和凯莉又在亲热了。

1362
00:56:22.250 --> 00:56:24.770
Oh, it's such a sloppy makeout, too.
噢，那亲热的样子真够邋遢的。

1363
00:56:25.010 --> 00:56:25.670
It is.
确实。

1364
00:56:25.910 --> 00:56:30.290
Not that a tidy makeout would have made it any better at work.
倒不是说在办公室里亲热得体面点就会好到哪去。

1365
00:56:30.830 --> 00:56:31.290
Exactly.
没错。

1366
00:56:31.950 --> 00:56:33.530
Well, Ryan wants out.
总之，瑞安想分手。

1367
00:56:33.650 --> 00:56:35.310
He doesn't want a sloppy makeout.
他不想再这样邋遢地亲热了。

1368
00:56:35.430 --> 00:56:36.530
He doesn't want a tidy one.
他连体面的亲热也不想要。

1369
00:56:36.690 --> 00:56:41.970
He's going to Thailand with some friends from high school, a high school.
他要和几个高中朋友去泰国，就是那种高中同学。

1370
00:56:42.510 --> 00:56:46.390
You know, he has to break up with her because if he doesn't, he'll always resent her.
你知道，他必须跟她分手，因为如果不分，他以后一定会怨恨她。

1371
00:56:46.470 --> 00:56:49.850
If he didn't go, he would like them to be adults about it.
如果他不走，他希望他们能成熟地处理这件事。

1372
00:56:50.070 --> 00:56:51.810
Maybe they could have sex one more time.
也许他们还能再做一次爱。

1373
00:56:51.970 --> 00:56:53.310
And does she have any cash?
而且她身上有现金吗？

1374
00:56:53.790 --> 00:56:56.770
Then let's be adults about it, but we could also have sex one more time.
那我们就成熟点处理，但我们还可以再做一次爱。

1375
00:56:56.890 --> 00:56:58.590
I think that's such a dude move.
我觉得这真是典型的男人行径。

1376
00:56:58.590 --> 00:57:00.590
I feel like I've heard that so many times.
我觉得这种话我听过太多次了。

1377
00:57:00.830 --> 00:57:01.510
I know.
我懂。

1378
00:57:01.810 --> 00:57:03.410
Do you want to have some goodbye sex?
你想来点告别性爱吗？

1379
00:57:03.690 --> 00:57:04.130
No.
不想。

1380
00:57:04.270 --> 00:57:05.610
No, just goodbye.
不，就只是告别。

1381
00:57:06.190 --> 00:57:08.270
Get your sorry ass out of here.
赶紧把你那倒霉样给我滚远点。

1382
00:57:08.750 --> 00:57:10.170
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1383
00:57:10.770 --> 00:57:11.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1384
00:57:11.410 --> 00:57:13.210
Fan question from Gracie R.
来自格雷西·R的粉丝提问。

1385
00:57:13.450 --> 00:57:19.810
When Ryan is telling Kelly he's going to Thailand, why are they both wearing different clothes?
当瑞安告诉凯莉他要去泰国时，为什么他们俩穿的衣服不一样？

1386
00:57:20.150 --> 00:57:21.710
I'll tell you, Gracie.
我来告诉你，格雷西。

1387
00:57:21.870 --> 00:57:28.330
Because this scene was originally supposed to be the tag at the end of the episode.
因为这个场景原本是打算作为剧集结尾的彩蛋。

1388
00:57:28.590 --> 00:57:30.790
And it was meant to be a new work day.
而且设定是在新的一天。

1389
00:57:30.990 --> 00:57:36.330
So in the script, this scene was not during the same day that we were framing Toby.
所以在剧本里，这场戏并不是在我们陷害托比的那一天发生的。

1390
00:57:36.610 --> 00:57:37.630
It was the next day.
那是第二天。

1391
00:57:37.810 --> 00:57:40.130
But in editing, they moved it up.
但在剪辑时，他们把它提前了。

1392
00:57:40.190 --> 00:57:45.930
And we are going to end instead with a delicious Dwight talking head.
而我们最后会以德怀特的一段精彩访谈作为结尾。

1393
00:57:46.130 --> 00:57:46.990
We'll get to it.
我们待会儿会讲到。

1394
00:57:47.150 --> 00:57:52.030
But first, Jim needs to show Pam what he's done.
但首先，吉姆得向帕姆展示他做了什么。

1395
00:57:52.530 --> 00:57:53.010
That's right.
没错。

1396
00:57:53.390 --> 00:57:54.730
Jim is nervous but excited.
吉姆既紧张又兴奋。

1397
00:57:54.730 --> 00:57:57.630
He is, as my daughter says, nervous-sided.
他就像我女儿说的那样，处于“紧张兴奋”状态。

1398
00:57:58.470 --> 00:58:01.210
And she's like, why are we stopping at your parents' house?
她当时问，我们为什么要停在你父母家门口？

1399
00:58:01.430 --> 00:58:03.850
And he says, I bought it.
他说，我把它买下来了。

1400
00:58:04.150 --> 00:58:08.470
And then Jenna, at 18 minutes, two seconds, Jim says, let's go inside.
然后珍娜，在18分02秒时，吉姆说，我们进去吧。

1401
00:58:08.470 --> 00:58:09.510
I'll show you inside.
我带你进去看看。

1402
00:58:09.850 --> 00:58:10.330
What?
什么？

1403
00:58:10.650 --> 00:58:12.730
Has Pam never been inside the house?
帕姆从来没进过这房子吗？

1404
00:58:12.910 --> 00:58:14.450
We got so much mail about that.
我们收到了好多关于这点的邮件。

1405
00:58:14.690 --> 00:58:15.630
People wrote in.
大家纷纷写信来问。

1406
00:58:15.630 --> 00:58:22.010
They said, if Pam knew they were at Jim's parents' house when they pulled up, wouldn't that mean she's been there before and she's probably been inside?
他们说，如果帕姆在车开到吉姆父母家时就知道那是哪儿，那不就意味着她以前去过，而且很可能进去过吗？

1407
00:58:22.310 --> 00:58:24.810
You would hope Pam has been inside his parents' house.
你确实会希望帕姆进过他父母的家。

1408
00:58:24.910 --> 00:58:25.870
They've been dating for a while.
他们交往有一阵子了。

1409
00:58:25.950 --> 00:58:27.010
They live in the same town.
他们住在同一个镇上。

1410
00:58:27.350 --> 00:58:27.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1411
00:58:27.770 --> 00:58:31.690
And it's interesting because his parents have moved out, but they've left some furniture.
而且很有趣的是，他父母已经搬走了，但留下了一些家具。

1412
00:58:31.970 --> 00:58:34.550
Also, how rough were they on this house?
另外，他们到底是怎么折腾这房子的？

1413
00:58:34.850 --> 00:58:35.550
I know.
我知道。

1414
00:58:35.550 --> 00:58:38.950
And Jim says, I was helping my mom out.
吉姆说，我在帮我妈忙。

1415
00:58:39.310 --> 00:58:40.310
Where's his dad?
他爸呢？

1416
00:58:40.550 --> 00:58:41.450
I don't know.
我不知道。

1417
00:58:41.610 --> 00:58:42.730
I have a lot of questions.
我有一堆疑问。

1418
00:58:43.030 --> 00:58:44.550
There were a lot of questions.
确实有很多疑问。

1419
00:58:44.910 --> 00:58:45.790
Rachel M.
瑞秋·M。

1420
00:58:45.950 --> 00:58:46.810
and Megan L.
和梅根·L。

1421
00:58:47.150 --> 00:58:48.750
said, question for Jenna.
说，有个问题想问珍娜。

1422
00:58:48.750 --> 00:58:56.570
In this episode, when Jim is showing Pam his parents' house, I was wondering, what went into how you decided to play this scene?
在这一集中，当吉姆带帕姆看他父母的房子时，我很好奇，你是怎么决定如何演绎这一幕的？

1423
00:58:56.850 --> 00:59:03.050
Because she seems really worried and unexcited, but then in the end, she says she loves it.
因为她看起来真的很担心，一点也不兴奋，但最后她却说她很喜欢。

1424
00:59:03.470 --> 00:59:09.670
Any input you could give about how you decided to play this or what the director told you would be super appreciated.
如果你能分享一下你是如何决定表演方式的，或者导演对你说了什么，我们将不胜感激。

1425
00:59:10.050 --> 00:59:17.390
Well, guys, we've already discussed my personal opinions on someone buying someone else a house without telling them.
好吧，各位，我们已经讨论过我对“在不告知对方的情况下买房”这件事的个人看法了。

1426
00:59:17.390 --> 00:59:28.770
So this was a little bit of a mental gymnastics for me to get Pam to the place where she's going to say she loves it and where she says that line.
所以对我来说，要让帕姆达到那种“说她很喜欢”并讲出那句台词的状态，需要进行一番心理博弈。

1427
00:59:28.970 --> 00:59:36.690
I mean, you bought me a house because it was like not how I would react as Jenna.
我是说，你给我买了一套房，这跟我作为珍娜本人的反应完全不同。

1428
00:59:36.930 --> 00:59:41.670
You know, I had to really play the character and play the character's truth.
你知道，我必须真正进入角色，演绎角色的真实感受。

1429
00:59:41.670 --> 00:59:50.530
And in the script, I was being told that my character's truth was that she loved this gesture and it made her feel loved.
剧本里告诉我，我角色的真实感受是她很喜欢这个举动，这让她感到被爱。

1430
00:59:51.090 --> 00:59:51.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1431
00:59:51.530 --> 00:59:53.250
Well, I mean, I think we often did that.
嗯，我是说，我觉得我们经常这样做。

1432
00:59:53.370 --> 00:59:55.330
Obviously, we had to play the truth for the character.
显然，我们必须演绎出角色的真实感受。

1433
00:59:55.670 --> 01:00:01.290
I mean, I hope you guys know I'm not very much like Angela Martin and how I would react to things.
我是说，我希望你们知道，我本人和安吉拉·马丁在面对事情时的反应大不相同。

1434
01:00:01.290 --> 01:00:10.850
But it made sense to me, Jenna, for Pam, you know, and Jim made the garage into this art studio and he's really putting down some roots with her.
但对我来说，珍娜，这对于帕姆是说得通的，你知道，吉姆把车库改成了艺术工作室，他真的在和她一起扎根生活。

1435
01:00:11.090 --> 01:00:17.670
And I think Pam wanted a family and she wanted all of these things that Jim is offering her.
而且我觉得帕姆想要一个家庭，她想要吉姆提供给她的这一切。

1436
01:00:17.870 --> 01:00:19.190
She had wanted that.
她一直渴望这些。

1437
01:00:19.750 --> 01:00:19.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1438
01:00:20.030 --> 01:00:30.230
You know, I had thought a little bit back on The Talking Head where Pam discusses what her perfect home would look like, how she always wanted a home with a terrace.
你知道，我回想了一下帕姆讨论她理想家园是什么样子的那个访谈片段，她一直想要一个带露台的家。

1439
01:00:31.470 --> 01:00:36.490
You know, picking her home seemed like something that Pam was attached to.
你知道，挑选自己的家似乎是帕姆很看重的事情。

1440
01:00:36.690 --> 01:00:38.430
So I did bring that up.
所以我确实提到了这一点。

1441
01:00:38.570 --> 01:00:45.330
I said, you know, we've established that Pam has daydreamed about what her home would look like.
我说，你知道，我们已经设定过帕姆曾幻想过自己的家是什么样子的。

1442
01:00:45.490 --> 01:00:49.030
And now this person has taken her out of the process.
而现在，这个人却把她排除在了这个过程之外。

1443
01:00:49.370 --> 01:00:52.770
You brought that up to the writers at the time of when we were filming?
你在拍摄的时候向编剧提过这一点吗？

1444
01:00:52.770 --> 01:00:53.330
Yeah.
提过。

1445
01:00:53.710 --> 01:01:01.370
And so I was saying, like, help me understand why Pam now is so happy and so excited.
所以我当时在说，帮我理解一下为什么帕姆现在会这么开心、这么兴奋。

1446
01:01:01.630 --> 01:01:10.970
And Angela, we got to exactly what you just said, which was that it was a vulnerable thing for Pam to give up the art school track.
安吉拉，我们得出了和你刚才说的一模一样的结论，那就是对于帕姆来说，放弃艺术学校的道路是一件很脆弱的事情。

1447
01:01:10.970 --> 01:01:14.750
And she did that because of two reasons.
她这样做有两个原因。

1448
01:01:15.130 --> 01:01:20.630
One, graphic design wasn't what she meant she wanted to do as an artiSt.
第一，平面设计并不是她作为艺术家真正想做的事情。

1449
01:01:20.910 --> 01:01:23.030
And two, she's ready.
第二，她准备好了。

1450
01:01:23.250 --> 01:01:35.530
She's very, very ready to start living this married life, to be in the season of family and marriage with this man that she's been waiting years for.
她非常、非常准备好开始这种婚姻生活了，准备好与这个她等待了多年的男人一起进入家庭和婚姻的阶段。

1451
01:01:35.530 --> 01:01:41.890
And so this home is her fast track to that season of her life.
所以这个家是她迈向人生新阶段的快车道。

1452
01:01:42.050 --> 01:01:43.110
And she's just ready.
而且她已经准备好了。

1453
01:01:43.970 --> 01:01:46.650
And, you know, they're going to get to fix it up together.
而且，你知道，他们可以一起装修这个家。

1454
01:01:46.650 --> 01:01:50.190
So there's still that element of nesting that's going to get to happen.
所以那种筑巢的感觉依然会存在。

1455
01:01:50.470 --> 01:01:55.490
And so that's kind of what I was thinking was like, I'm ready.
所以我当时想的就是，我已经准备好了。

1456
01:01:55.490 --> 01:01:56.170
Yeah.
没错。

1457
01:01:56.390 --> 01:02:05.870
And you have to think when Pam talked about her dream house with this tower and the terrace and all of that, she was in an unhappy relationship.
你得想想，当帕姆谈论她梦想中的房子，有塔楼、露台还有其他那些东西时，她正处于一段不幸福的关系中。

1458
01:02:05.970 --> 01:02:15.210
When you're in a place you feel stuck in life or you're unhappy, you daydream and you daydream about these fantastical things and their coping mechanisMs.
当你觉得生活受困或不快乐时，你会做白日梦，幻想那些虚无缥缈的东西，那是你的应对机制。

1459
01:02:15.630 --> 01:02:20.790
And then when you're with someone you really love, you don't need the fantasy anymore.
而当你和真正爱的人在一起时，你就不再需要那些幻想了。

1460
01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:22.910
That's such a good point, Angela.
安吉拉，你说得太对了。

1461
01:02:23.210 --> 01:02:24.590
You're just ready to have a life.
你只是准备好去过真正的生活了。

1462
01:02:24.590 --> 01:02:26.670
And she's ready to have that life.
而她也准备好去过那种生活了。

1463
01:02:27.170 --> 01:02:27.290
Yeah.
没错。

1464
01:02:27.730 --> 01:02:30.030
Now, we did get some mail about that garage.
现在，我们收到了一些关于那个车库的来信。

1465
01:02:30.870 --> 01:02:31.390
Katie C.
凯蒂·C.

1466
01:02:31.550 --> 01:02:32.270
and Chris G.
和克里斯·G.

1467
01:02:32.490 --> 01:02:32.770
said,
说，

1468
01:02:32.910 --> 01:02:37.330
When Jim is showing Pam his parents' house, he says the garage has great lighting.
当吉姆带帕姆看他父母的房子时，他说车库采光很好。

1469
01:02:37.750 --> 01:02:43.730
He then proceeds to open a windowless garage door, revealing a completely windowless garage space.
接着他打开了一扇没有窗户的车库门，露出了一个完全没有窗户的车库空间。

1470
01:02:44.050 --> 01:02:45.630
Where's the great lighting, Jim?
吉姆，采光好的地方在哪儿呢？

1471
01:02:45.970 --> 01:02:46.350
Where?
在哪儿？

1472
01:02:46.770 --> 01:02:48.650
Okay, well, I thought that was really funny.
好吧，我觉得这真的很好笑。

1473
01:02:49.070 --> 01:02:50.250
That is really funny.
确实很好笑。

1474
01:02:50.250 --> 01:02:55.010
I want you guys to know that I have a garage that we use as a home office.
我想让你们知道，我有一个车库，我们把它当成家庭办公室用。

1475
01:02:55.590 --> 01:02:58.970
And for a long time, we would just raise the door.
很长一段时间里，我们只是把门拉开。

1476
01:02:59.110 --> 01:03:01.210
And then there would be amazing light.
然后就会有很棒的光线照进来。

1477
01:03:01.530 --> 01:03:01.830
You know?
你懂吗？

1478
01:03:02.130 --> 01:03:02.530
Yeah.
懂。

1479
01:03:02.550 --> 01:03:05.930
So it did get great light, but you had to raise the door.
所以它的采光确实很好，但你得把门拉开。

1480
01:03:05.930 --> 01:03:12.090
And then years later, we actually just removed the door because we're like, this is never going to be a garage again.
后来过了几年，我们干脆把门拆了，因为我们觉得，这永远不会再是个车库了。

1481
01:03:12.370 --> 01:03:17.030
You know, we've sort of made it into this little home office and put an actual sliding glass door.
你知道，我们把它改造成了一个小小的家庭办公室，还装了一扇真正的推拉玻璃门。

1482
01:03:17.350 --> 01:03:18.850
But I get it.
但我明白你们的意思。

1483
01:03:18.850 --> 01:03:20.170
It does have great lighting.
它的采光确实很好。

1484
01:03:20.310 --> 01:03:21.590
You just have to open it up.
你只需要把它打开就行。

1485
01:03:21.590 --> 01:03:33.190
But he does present it like this garage has great lighting, as if the other garages that you open, the whole side of the building, wouldn't have great lighting.
但他表现得好像这个车库采光特别好，仿佛其他车库只要把整面墙打开，就不会有这么好的采光一样。

1486
01:03:33.310 --> 01:03:41.450
He's presenting as if it's like a special feature that kind of applies to every garage that doesn't have like a giant tree planted in front of it,
他表现得好像这是一种特殊功能，其实只要前面没种棵大树，每个车库都这样，

1487
01:03:41.570 --> 01:03:43.310
which it wouldn't because it's a garage.
本来就该这样，因为那是车库。

1488
01:03:43.590 --> 01:03:43.810
Right.
没错。

1489
01:03:43.990 --> 01:03:46.350
Most garages are just boxes with no windows.
大多数车库都只是没有窗户的盒子。

1490
01:03:47.110 --> 01:03:50.610
I have to tell you two things about shooting these scenes at the house.
关于在房子里拍这些戏份，我有两件事要告诉你们。

1491
01:03:50.850 --> 01:03:59.710
The scene where Jim is trying to take the clown painting off the wall for Pam is one of the hardest I've ever laughed on the show.
吉姆试图帮帕姆把墙上的小丑画取下来的那场戏，是我拍这部剧时笑得最厉害的场景之一。

1492
01:03:59.870 --> 01:04:01.590
It is the second hardest time.
这是我笑得第二厉害的一次。

1493
01:04:01.790 --> 01:04:07.570
The first was when we did the scene in Dinner Party where Michael's showing us the tiny TV on the wall.
第一次是拍《晚宴》那集，迈克尔给我们展示墙上那个超小电视的时候。

1494
01:04:08.530 --> 01:04:09.710
This is the second.
这是第二次。

1495
01:04:10.650 --> 01:04:16.230
Every time John tried to lift the painting on the wall, I could not stop laughing.
每次约翰试图把墙上的画取下来，我就忍不住大笑。

1496
01:04:16.350 --> 01:04:17.730
I don't know what it was.
我不知道为什么。

1497
01:04:18.050 --> 01:04:18.570
Tears.
眼泪都出来了。

1498
01:04:18.770 --> 01:04:19.290
Tears.
眼泪。

1499
01:04:19.630 --> 01:04:21.030
Choking on our laughter.
笑得喘不过气。

1500
01:04:21.410 --> 01:04:22.690
We laughed so hard.
我们笑得太厉害了。

1501
01:04:22.950 --> 01:04:25.910
I looked for it in the bloopers, and it's not there.
我在花絮里找过，但没找到。

1502
01:04:25.950 --> 01:04:27.730
And I'm so upset it's not there.
没找到我真的好难过。

1503
01:04:27.870 --> 01:04:35.150
It took us like an hour to shoot that tiny moment of him trying to take the painting off the wall.
他试图把那幅画从墙上取下来，就那么一小会儿，我们拍了大概一个小时。

1504
01:04:35.390 --> 01:04:38.170
John is also so funny at physical comedy.
约翰在肢体喜剧方面也很有天赋。

1505
01:04:38.550 --> 01:04:38.990
Yes.
没错。

1506
01:04:39.170 --> 01:04:43.650
I laughed out loud when he peeled back that fake wood paneling, and it kind of startled him.
他揭开那块假木镶板时吓了一跳，我当时直接笑出声了。

1507
01:04:43.890 --> 01:04:44.330
Yes.
是啊。

1508
01:04:44.330 --> 01:04:52.650
So then at the end of the scene in the garage, when we're hugging, I improvised the line, what about the clown?
所以后来在车库那场戏结束时，我们拥抱的时候，我即兴加了一句台词：那小丑画怎么办？

1509
01:04:53.010 --> 01:04:57.770
And it made John laugh, and that's why he's like burying his head into my neck.
这把约翰逗笑了，所以他才把头埋进我的脖子里。

1510
01:04:57.770 --> 01:05:03.410
And then when he said, yeah, I can't do anything about that, it made me laugh.
然后他说：是啊，我对此无能为力，这又把我逗笑了。

1511
01:05:03.450 --> 01:05:06.050
And so I'm like smushing my face into his shoulder.
所以我当时就把脸埋进了他的肩膀里。

1512
01:05:06.330 --> 01:05:07.710
You can totally tell we're breaking.
你能明显看出我们当时笑场了。

1513
01:05:08.030 --> 01:05:13.970
And that's why it was because we were still, anytime we brought up the clown painting, we lost it.
就是因为我们当时只要一提到那幅小丑画，就忍不住笑场。

1514
01:05:13.970 --> 01:05:15.750
But I loved that moment.
但我很喜欢那一刻。

1515
01:05:15.930 --> 01:05:18.250
It made it intimate and funny and sweet.
它既亲密又好笑，还很甜蜜。

1516
01:05:18.650 --> 01:05:22.390
I think it's time to talk about the greatest Dwight talking head of all time.
我觉得是时候聊聊德怀特有史以来最棒的单人访谈了。

1517
01:05:22.390 --> 01:05:29.870
That's saying a lot, because there are some amazing Dwight talking heads, but this one really is like top five.
这评价很高，因为德怀特的精彩访谈有很多，但这一段绝对能排进前五。

1518
01:05:30.110 --> 01:05:34.210
He's going to describe his perfect crime, and I think we have to hear it.
他要描述他的完美犯罪了，我觉得我们必须听听。

1519
01:05:34.850 --> 01:05:36.030
What is my perfect crime?
什么是我的完美犯罪？

1520
01:05:36.650 --> 01:05:38.270
I break into Tiffany's at midnight.
我在午夜潜入蒂芙尼珠宝店。

1521
01:05:38.810 --> 01:05:39.930
Do I go for the vault?
我会去保险库吗？

1522
01:05:40.130 --> 01:05:40.310
No.
不会。

1523
01:05:40.490 --> 01:05:41.610
I go for the chandelier.
我会去拿那盏吊灯。

1524
01:05:41.770 --> 01:05:42.350
It's priceless.
那是无价之宝。

1525
01:05:42.890 --> 01:05:45.010
As I'm taking it down, a woman catches me.
当我把它取下来时，一个女人抓住了我。

1526
01:05:45.170 --> 01:05:46.230
She tells me to stop.
她让我住手。

1527
01:05:46.450 --> 01:05:47.610
It's her father's business.
那是她父亲的生意。

1528
01:05:47.830 --> 01:05:48.450
She's Tiffany.
她就是蒂芙尼本人。

1529
01:05:48.730 --> 01:05:49.430
I say no.
我说不。

1530
01:05:49.650 --> 01:05:50.730
We make love all night.
我们整晚都在缠绵。

1531
01:05:50.930 --> 01:05:53.830
In the morning, the cops come, and I escape in one of their uniforMs.
早上警察来了，我穿着他们的制服逃走了。

1532
01:05:53.830 --> 01:05:56.710
I tell her to meet me in Mexico, but I go to Canada.
我让她去墨西哥见我，但我去了加拿大。

1533
01:05:56.930 --> 01:05:57.810
I don't trust her.
我不信任她。

1534
01:05:58.270 --> 01:05:59.550
Besides, I like the cold.
再说，我喜欢寒冷。

1535
01:06:00.490 --> 01:06:01.910
Thirty years later, I get a postcard.
三十年后，我收到了一张明信片。

1536
01:06:02.110 --> 01:06:04.290
I have a son, and he's the chief of police.
我有个儿子，他是警察局长。

1537
01:06:04.590 --> 01:06:06.050
This is where the story gets interesting.
故事精彩的地方来了。

1538
01:06:06.430 --> 01:06:09.490
I tell Tiffany to meet me in Paris by the Trocadero.
我让蒂芙尼去巴黎的特罗卡德罗广场见我。

1539
01:06:10.390 --> 01:06:12.010
She's been waiting for me all these years.
这些年来她一直都在等我。

1540
01:06:12.130 --> 01:06:13.230
She's never taken another lover.
她从未找过其他情人。

1541
01:06:13.490 --> 01:06:14.250
I don't care.
我不在乎。

1542
01:06:14.390 --> 01:06:15.030
I don't show up.
我没去。

1543
01:06:15.110 --> 01:06:15.730
I go to Berlin.
我去了柏林。

1544
01:06:16.050 --> 01:06:17.830
That's where I stashed the chandelier.
那是我藏吊灯的地方。

1545
01:06:19.070 --> 01:06:19.470
Yeah.
没错。

1546
01:06:19.730 --> 01:06:23.270
I do not know how Rain got through saying,
我不知道雷恩是怎么忍住不笑说完那句的，

1547
01:06:23.830 --> 01:06:25.390
this is where the story gets interesting.
故事精彩的地方来了。

1548
01:06:26.050 --> 01:06:26.950
I know.
我知道。

1549
01:06:28.420 --> 01:06:30.840
When I watched this episode, I laughed at that line,
我看这一集的时候，被那句台词逗笑了，

1550
01:06:30.960 --> 01:06:32.320
and I watched it like three times.
我大概看了三遍。

1551
01:06:32.540 --> 01:06:35.020
This entire talking head was scripted,
这段访谈完全是有剧本的，

1552
01:06:35.160 --> 01:06:37.140
and it was delivered as scripted.
而且是照着剧本念的。

1553
01:06:37.280 --> 01:06:40.940
I think this is one of the most brilliantly written pieces ever.
我认为这是有史以来写得最精彩的片段之一。

1554
01:06:41.300 --> 01:06:42.880
It's just so good.
真的太棒了。

1555
01:06:43.200 --> 01:06:47.400
It's so good, and who better to deliver it than Rainn Wilson as Dwight?
太棒了，而且还有谁比雷恩·威尔森饰演的德怀特更适合演绎这段呢？

1556
01:06:47.560 --> 01:06:49.020
It was just perfect.
简直完美。

1557
01:06:49.380 --> 01:06:50.140
I agree.
我同意。

1558
01:06:50.600 --> 01:06:51.920
There you have it, everyone.
大家听到了吧。

1559
01:06:51.920 --> 01:06:52.980
That's frame Toby.
那就是陷害托比。

1560
01:06:53.340 --> 01:06:54.520
Did you have anything else, Angela?
你还有什么要说的吗，安吉拉？

1561
01:06:54.520 --> 01:06:56.360
I don't have anything else.
我没什么要说的了。

1562
01:06:56.360 --> 01:06:57.760
I do want you guys to know,
我确实想让你们知道，

1563
01:06:57.920 --> 01:06:59.640
because Jenna and I both watched the bloopers,
因为珍娜和我都在看花絮，

1564
01:07:00.200 --> 01:07:04.780
next week on The Surplus was one of the hardest I've ever laughed in a scene.
下周要讲的《剩余物资》那一集，是我拍戏时笑得最厉害的一次。

1565
01:07:05.120 --> 01:07:06.120
Oh, I can't wait.
噢，我等不及了。

1566
01:07:06.640 --> 01:07:10.340
Thank you so much to Randy Cordray, James Carey,
非常感谢兰迪·科德雷、詹姆斯·凯里，

1567
01:07:10.460 --> 01:07:12.460
and Jen Salata and Paul Lieberstein.
还有珍·萨拉塔和保罗·李伯斯汀。

1568
01:07:12.580 --> 01:07:14.160
I traded some emails with them as well.
我也和他们互通了一些邮件。

1569
01:07:14.640 --> 01:07:15.840
Man, that was fun.
天哪，那太有趣了。

1570
01:07:16.100 --> 01:07:17.220
That was a delight.
那真是太令人愉快了。

1571
01:07:17.480 --> 01:07:21.180
I will be trying to clean my microwave using your method.
我会试着用你的方法清理我的微波炉。

1572
01:07:21.180 --> 01:07:22.400
Thank you.
谢谢。

1573
01:07:23.140 --> 01:07:25.800
And we'll see you here next week.
我们下周再见。

1574
01:07:26.000 --> 01:07:27.660
I'll be back in LA next week.
我下周会回到洛杉矶。

1575
01:07:27.800 --> 01:07:30.580
I wonder, will I bring New York Jenna home with me?
我在想，我会把“纽约珍娜”带回家吗？

1576
01:07:30.740 --> 01:07:31.100
We'll see.
走着瞧吧。

1577
01:07:31.740 --> 01:07:32.220
I don't know.
我不知道。

1578
01:07:32.320 --> 01:07:35.040
New York Jenna might put the E next to our podcaSt.
“纽约珍娜”可能会把那个E字母加到我们的播客标题里。

1579
01:07:35.600 --> 01:07:36.080
Sorry.
抱歉。

1580
01:07:37.040 --> 01:07:38.020
What can I say?
我能说什么呢？

1581
01:07:39.740 --> 01:07:40.940
See you next week, guys.
下周见，伙计们。

1582
01:07:41.240 --> 01:07:42.120
See you next week.
下周见。

1583
01:07:42.120 --> 01:07:47.170
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1584
01:07:47.430 --> 01:07:50.910
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Earwolf、珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1585
